    "chunk_size_bytes": 1831,
    "chunk_text": "Cabinet approves Rs. 800 m equity injection for Lanka Metro Transit\n\nGrants additional Rs.267.5 m equity capital for company\u2019s operations in 2027\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers has approved an equity capital allocation of Rs. 800 million to Lanka Metro Transit Ltd., to develop infrastructure required to expand modern public transport operations in Colombo and surrounding areas.\n\nIn addition, the Cabinet approved Rs. 267.5 million in equity capital for the company\u2019s operations in 2027, indicating that the Government views the pilot as a viable model for wider urban transport operations.\n\nLanka Metro Transit Ltd., was incorporated on 3 October 2025, as a subsidiary of the Sri Lanka Transport Board (SLTB) under the Companies Act No. 7 of 2007, with the objective of supporting the modernisation of Sri Lanka\u2019s public transport system.\n\nThe company has already commenced a Colombo Urban Transport Pilot Operation, using 10 low-floor buses purchased with funding allocated under the Clean Sri Lanka Program.\n\nAccording to the Government, the pilot operation has demonstrated both the commercial feasibility and public acceptance of the service, prompting the company to expand its operations.\n\nAs part of the planned expansion, 112 additional low-floor buses are scheduled to be introduced in September, significantly increasing the scale of the modern bus service.\n\nHowever, the expansion has also highlighted the need for supporting infrastructure to ensure that the new fleet can be operated efficiently and systematically.\n\nThe proposed infrastructure development includes the construction of a fully equipped central workshop, as well as modern bus depots at Thalangama, Kadawatha, Ratmalana and Homagama. The programme will also include improvements to internal roads and the construction and development of bus stands."
