    "md5": "e0d61762db5b3a5aebfc43fb8e772bff",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1343,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe private sector has a critical role to play in shaping economies that are resilient, inclusive and sustainable. As businesses navigate a rapidly changing global landscape, responsible business is increasingly central to competitiveness, trust and long-term value creation.\u201d\n\nShe said the UN Global Compact\u2019s Ten Principles provided the companies with a framework to convert the sustainability commitments into action. The principles cover human rights, labour, environment and anti-corruption.\n\nCSE CEO Rajeeva Bandaranaike said responsible corporate conduct, transparency and strong governance were fundamental to investor confidence and resilient economic growth.\n\n\u201cThe Responsible Business Coalition provides an important platform for bringing together businesses and professional institutions around a shared commitment to sustainability and responsible corporate conduct,\u201d he said.\n\nThe coalition will seek to use the reach of its participating business and professional associations to provide current and future corporate leaders with knowledge, tools and partnerships to improve responsible business practices.\n\nThe bell-ringing event forms part of an international initiative involving the UN Sustainable Stock Exchanges Initiative, UN Global Compact, International Finance Corporation and World Federation of Exchanges."
