    "chunk_text": "Q While your party complained against the 22nd Amendment to the Constitution, those supporting the government argue that the culture of interfering with the judiciary and the chief justice started from the time of J. R. Jayewardene, the leader of your mother party UNP and the procedure was followed by Chandrika\u2019s government and then byMahinda Rajapaksa. What is your say?\n\nThe power of the Executive lies with the JVP, 2/3rd of the legislature lies with them. Why are they extending the retirement age only in the judiciary in a context where they have failed to recruit the required officials for the vacant positions\n\nOne Minister of the government stated during a recently held press conference that there will be no more Presidential Elections held by the Government. This means either they have to amend the Constitution or drag the country towards a dictatorship. People need to act to protect their democratic rights. We challenge the government that if they are popular and that people are fond of them, to do an investigation and conduct Provincial Council Elections."
