    "description": "Sri Lanka, EU convene high-level investment dialogue in Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Sri-Lanka-EU-convene-high-level-investment-dialogue-in-Colombo/34-795923",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1786580934.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-13-dailyftlk-d6263214-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "bf86ee8f5ef4befd2ba6a8d8f9ff859e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1474,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka, EU convene high-level investment dialogue in Colombo\n\nMinisterial-level talks address investment climate reforms, market access and a deeper European\u2013Sri Lanka partnership\n\nThe Government of Sri Lanka and the European Union (EU) recently held the Sri Lanka-European Union Investment Dialogue; a high-level policy engagement convened in Colombo.\n\nThe session brought together senior Sri Lankan Government officials, EU Ambassador to Sri Lanka and the Maldives, and Ambassadors of France, Germany, Italy, and the Netherlands, and representatives of EU Member States missions for a structured conversation on investment facilitation, policy consistency and the future of European\u2013Sri Lankan economic cooperation.\n\nThe Dialogue is the latest session of the Sri Lanka-EU Investor Dialogue, first established in 2014 to maintain regular, structured communication between the European Embassies and the Government of Sri Lanka. This session was convened at the ministerial level, reflecting the importance both sides attach to sustaining investor confidence as Sri Lanka continues its post-crisis recovery under its IMF-supported reform programme.\n\nFollowing the presentation of an independent Investment Climate Assessment, the Dialogue focused on Sri Lanka\u2019s strategic choice on foreign investment; translating that vision into implementation through regulatory reform; and identifying opportunities to build a deeper European\u2013Sri Lanka investment partnership."
  },
