    "md5": "176f85653805d578c44bffaad4cf987e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1866,
    "chunk_text": "ProFood ProPack and AgBiz 23rd edition from 21 Aug.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s premium exhibition for the food processing, packaging, and agriculture sectors, ProFood ProPack and AgBiz 2026, will return to BMICH from 21 to 23 August 2026, bringing together local and international industry leaders, innovators, entrepreneurs, and consumers for knowledge exchange, innovation, and business networking.\n\nOrganised by the Sri Lanka Food Processors Association (SLFPA) together with the professional exhibition organiser, Lanka Exhibition and Conference Services Ltd., the three-day exhibition is expected to attract more than 30,000 trade and consumer visitors, while featuring over 450 exhibition stalls spread across 6 exhibition halls. The event will host over 50 international exhibitors and participants representing countries including China, India, and Germany, strengthening its position as one of the region\u2019s leading industry platforms.\n\nInitiated to serve both business-to-consumer (B2C) and business-to-business (B2B) audiences, ProFood ProPack and AgBiz 2026 will connect packaging specialists, exporters, retailers, manufacturers, food processors, distributors, entrepreneurs, investors, and the public, creating valuable opportunities for networking, knowledge sharing, and business growth.\n\nSLFPA President Aruna Senanayake said: \u201cWe remain deeply committed to supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s small and medium-scale food processors, who represent the backbone of our industry. The SME Pavilion, organised by the Industries Ministry has attracted a significant number of SMEs in previous years and provided tremendous support by bringing together many SME exhibitors under one roof for this mega event. This exhibition will provide SMEs with a valuable opportunity to showcase their innovations, gain market exposure and receive valuable feedback from end consumers.\u201d"
  },
