    "chunk_text": "Nanayakkara also expressed appreciation for more than 9,000 voluntary mediators across the country, who contribute their time and expertise without financial expectations to help resolve disputes and promote peaceful settlements.\n\nShe said the Ministry plans to expand child-friendly mediation programmes, special land mediation boards and financial dispute resolution boards nationwide to further promote a culture of mediation.\n\nJinasena also said that the Civil and Commercial Disputes Act has been passed by Parliament to establish a modern legal framework for commercial and business disputes in line with international standards, while ensuring equal access to justice across Sri Lanka\u2019s multicultural communities."
