    "chunk_text": "Opening the forum, Sri Lankan High Commissioner to the Maldives Mohamed Rizvi Hassen set the tone for a morning of substantive dialogue, reflecting on the depth and natural complementarity of the Sri Lanka\u2013Maldives bilateral relationship. He noted that Sri Lanka and the Maldives are among the Indian Ocean\u2019s closest neighbours connected by geography, culture, and longstanding people-to-people ties, and that Port City Colombo represents a tangible and timely opportunity to translate that relationship into a new dimension of economic partnership.\n\nSharing his first-hand experience of Port City Colombo, Riyaz offered a direct endorsement that resonated with the audience. \u201cPort City Colombo deserves our attention because it represents more than a real estate development. It represents an ambition to create a new economic platform within our immediate neighbourhood,\u201d he said. \u201cFrom Mal\u00e9 to Colombo is a short flight, and there is already a high level of familiarity between our banking systems, our business communities, and our people. I am in Colombo practically every other month, and I have seen how Port City Colombo started and how today, the utilities are connected to the main grid, office spaces occupied, and a duty-free mall is in operation. Every time I visit, there is something different. Investor confidence is built through implementation - and that is exactly what we are seeing. My message today is that every serious investor should explore the opportunities at Port City Colombo.\u201d\n\nThe centre-piece of the forum was a detailed presentation by the Port City Colombo team, delivered across three segments covering the broader Port City Colombo development story, the land and real estate investment opportunities available within the SEZ, and the business setup proposition for companies considering establishing operations at Port City Colombo."
