    "md5": "2b0473c124c00440c0513566f6a79d3f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1509,
    "chunk_text": "AIA Poson Safety Programme marks another year of impact\n\nReinforcing a 31-year commitment to safeguarding Sri Lankans, AIA Insurance Lanka expanded its annual Poson safety programme this year with a range of initiatives to support safer, healthier and more convenient pilgrimage experiences for hundreds of thousands of devotees visiting Anuradhapura and Mihintale.\n\nFor over three decades, the AIA Poson Safety Programme has been a trusted presence of the Poson season in Anuradhapura. This year, it brought together public safety, health awareness, environmental stewardship and transport assistance under one integrated initiative.\n\nAs part of this year\u2019s enhanced initiative, AIA Insurance operated a free Poson Pilgrimage Train from Colombo Fort to Anuradhapura, enabling approximately 1,500 devotees to travel to the sacred city safely and conveniently. To further facilitate movement between key pilgrimage sites, a free shuttle train service was introduced between Anuradhapura and Mihintale for three consecutive days, providing transport for approximately 22,000 passengers.\n\nRecognising the importance of safety during the Poson season, AIA Insurance once again partnered with the Sri Lanka Police, Sri Lanka Life Saving Association, Sri Lanka Navy and the Civil Security Department to deploy more than 530 lifeguards across 44 reservoirs and water bodies in Anuradhapura and surrounding areas. This year alone, the programme helped save six lives, further strengthening its long-standing impact."
  },
