    "md5": "2d5983c0f0ade78cd01f1e4041855dd7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1736,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys Alumex supports expressway reforestation project\n\nParticipants and volunteers from Hayleys Alumex come together along expressway green corridor to plant and tag indigenous tree saplings as part of their environmental reforestation initiative\n\nHayleys Alumex PLC, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading aluminium extrusion manufacturer, partnered with the Road Development Authority and Operations and Maintenance Management Division of the Southern Expressway, to plant approximately 600 indigenous and fruit-bearing trees along sections of the Southern Expressway \u2013 spanning the Galanigama and Meerigama-Kurunegala Expressways.\n\nThe initiative, which included species such as mee, kubuk and kaha karanda, reflects the company\u2019s broader sustainability agenda by minimising its environmental footprint while restoring Sri Lanka\u2019s natural ecosystems through collaborative partnerships.\n\nBy increasing indigenous tree cover, the project contributes to restoring ecological balance in the areas affected by infrastructure development while supporting long-term biodiversity conservation.\n\nIt will also help create greener transport corridors, enhancing both the surrounding landscape and the overall driving environment by reducing visual monotony for the motorists.\n\n\u201cHayleys Alumex is pleased to work with the Road Development Authority in restoring tree cover along vital expressways to leave a lasting environmental legacy. Meaningful environmental progress comes from partnerships and a shared commitment to improving public spaces. As a manufacturer, we believe contributing to the environment in the communities where we operate is simply part of being a responsible business,\u201d said Hayleys Alumex Managing Director Pramuk Dediwela."
