    "chunk_text": "The forums will be conducted amidst a remarkable six-year growth in the capital market, which saw the ASPI rise from 4,846 points in May 2020 to 22,310.80 points by end-May 2026. This represents a growth of 360 percent and a compound annual growth rate of approximately 28.98 percent.\n\nCommenting on Sri Lanka\u2019s investment landscape and the importance of engaging with international investors, SEC Chairman Senior Prof. D.B.P.H. Dissabandara, stated, \u201cSri Lanka is strengthening its capital market through robust regulation, greater transparency and stronger investor protection, creating a more trusted and resilient environment for investors. We invite the Australian investors to explore the opportunities emerging in our market.\u201d\n\nHigh-level government officials, regulators, listed companies, leading stockbroking firms and international investors will convene at the forum, to foster connections and promote long-term capital flows into Sri Lanka.\n\nCSE Executive Vice President Marketing Niroshan Wijesundere commented that there is a strong interest in the forums, with the registrations for several sessions already exceeding capacity.\n\nCHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt.) Ltd is participating in the Invest Sri Lanka investor forums in Australia as a collaborative partner, joining the SEC and CSE in bringing Sri Lanka\u2019s investment proposition to the Australian investors and businesses.\n\n\u201cAustralia represents a significant market for Sri Lanka and this forum provides a timely platform to engage directly with the investors who are well-positioned to recognise the opportunity. We look forward to sharing what Port City Colombo has to offer as part of Sri Lanka\u2019s broader investment story,\u201d stated CHEC Port City Colombo Managing Director Xiong Hongfeng.\n\nThe Board of Investment of Sri Lanka will also be participating in the forums, further strengthening the representation of key stakeholders driving the country\u2019s investment and economic development agenda."
