    "md5": "9247bfed3b7b61f1a89072fd94bdb1e5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1783,
    "chunk_text": "Ceylon Hotels Corporation marks 60 years\n\nCeylon Hotels Corporation PLC (CHC) is celebrating its 60th anniversary in 2026, marking six decades of hospitality and its contribution to the development and evolution of Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism industry.\n\nEstablished in 1966, under Ceylon Hotels Corporation Act No. 14 of 1966, CHC emerged at a defining stage in the country\u2019s tourism journey, when Sri Lanka was beginning to develop the infrastructure required to establish itself as an international tourism destination.\n\nFrom its early years, CHC played an important role in extending hospitality beyond the country\u2019s established cities into the hill country, ancient kingdoms, wildlife regions and coastal destinations. Its historic rest houses became familiar landmarks for generations of local and international travellers, offering accommodation as well as an introduction to Sri Lankan food, culture and hospitality.\n\nToday, CHC\u2019s portfolio brings together EKHO Hotels & Resorts, Queen\u2019s Hotel and Hotel Suisse in Kandy and Heritage Collection, with properties located across some of Sri Lanka\u2019s most culturally, historically and naturally significant destinations.\n\nCoinciding with its 60th anniversary, CHC is entering a new phase of investment, aimed at preserving the character of its historic properties while enhancing the overall hospitality experience for a new generation of travellers.\n\nThe historic Pussellawa Rest House has undergone renovations as part of this renewed focus, while the rest houses in Belihuloya and Kithulgala are currently being reimagined to offer an elevated hospitality experience while retaining their strong connection to their respective destinations and heritage. Both properties are scheduled to reopen to the public in October 2026."
  },
