    "chunk_text": "\u200bThe management transition aligns with the government\u2019s broader policy on the national carrier. Despite the airline\u2019s historic financial difficulties, state policy firmly emphasises the necessity of maintaining a national airline due to its critical role in supporting the local economy, driving the tourism sector, and serving vital national interests during emergencies.\n\n\u200b\u201cWe have appointed a group led by Dr. Wijayasuriya to analyse how this restructuring model should function,\u201d Kodithuwakku explained. \u201cThey are looking deeply into whether we retain the majority shareholding under the government while exploring options for capital injections, or whether we should pursue a management contract. They have about five months to submit their report, and the final restructuring process for SriLankan Airlines will be decided based on those findings.\u201d\n\n\u200bThe government has already begun receiving strategic restructuring proposals from foreign entities, including a recent submission from Hong Kong-based Transwell.\u00a0 . These plans are being forwarded directly to the committee for evaluation. Kodithuwakku claimed that despite ongoing financial constraints and the lack of a permanent CEO, the airline\u2019s staff have successfully managed operations and maintained critical flight slots, highlighting the urgent need for a stabilised, long-term corporate framework."
