    "chunk_text": "CCID obtains 90-day detention order for drug trafficker Shiran Basik\n\nColombo, Aug. 17 (Daily Mirror) - The Central Criminal Investigation Department (CCID) has obtained approval to detain 48-year-old drug trafficker Shiran Basik for 90 days.\n\nBasik, a resident of Dehiwala, was arrested in Dubai and brought back to Sri Lanka on August 14, according to Police.\n\nHe was arrested by officers of the Criminal Investigation Department\u2019s Airport Unit upon arrival at Bandaranaike International Airport and subsequently handed over to the CCID for further questioning.\n\nAccording to reports, Basik told investigators that he was stopped and questioned by Dubai police while at a luxury shopping complex during a period when the emirate was experiencing continuous attacks from Iran.\n\nHe reportedly claimed that police examined his mobile phone and found images related to the Iranian strikes, which led to his arrest.\n\nBasik further alleged that Dubai police questioned him daily until his deportation, mainly over possible links to Iran."
