    "md5": "9244e54d6dc41b4e759d43d9de17c484",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1985,
    "chunk_text": "Sheraton Colombo elevates culinary landscape with authentic Mughlai heritage festival\n\nA recent visit to Sheraton Colombo revealed a dining experience that is both a treat for the palate and a sophisticated cultural journey. The hotel, in a significant partnership with JW Marriott Bengaluru, is hosting \u2018An Ode To Mughlai Heritage\u2019 at its Colombo Kitchen restaurant.\n\nDesigned as a vibrant all-day dining destination inspired by a modern gourmet market, Colombo Kitchen is proving to be an ideal setting where food meets culture, providing a space for the diners to explore global flavours in a contemporary atmosphere.\n\nThis collaborative event, running from August 14 to 23, between 7:00 p.m. and 10:30 p.m., is a clear indication of Sheraton Colombo\u2019s commitment to reviving Colombo\u2019s dining scene.\n\nThe property has been actively transforming the city\u2019s culinary landscape by bringing in specialised international expertise to stimulate the local market. This follows their highly successful \u2018Spice Trails of Malaysia\u2019 festival in June and July, where they collaborated with Le M\u00e9ridien Kuala Lumpur and the High Commission of Malaysia to showcase the authentic regional gastronomy.\n\nAlongside other recent initiatives like the Jaffna Food Festival, Sheraton Colombo is strategically positioning itself as a premier hub for diverse, world-class culinary events.\n\nThe Mughlai festival masterfully captures the essence of this historic cuisine, known for its rich flavours and intricate preparation. The centrepiece and perhaps the most exciting aspect for biryani aficionados, is the rotating selection of regional biryanis.\n\n\u201cWe wanted to do something different and give our customers the opportunity to experience different types of biryani and flavours from across the region,\u201d the Sheraton Colombo executive chef explained.\n\n\u201cOver the 10 days, we will rotate five varieties, including Lucknow, Hyderabadi, Mumbai, Donne from Karnataka and Delhi biryani.\u201d"
  },
