    "md5": "aa25014ee5282f65ba3f160b521a327c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1883,
    "chunk_text": "Browns Hotels & Resorts launches Learning Academy\n\nBrowns Hotels & Resorts management team with first batch of Learning Academy\n\nLaunch ceremony of Browns Hotels & Resorts Learning Academy at The Eden Beruwala\n\nThe next generation of hospitality professionals now has a new place to learn, train and build their careers, as Browns Hotels & Resorts (BHR) launches the Browns Hotels & Resorts Learning Academy at The Eden Beruwala.\n\nDesigned to bridge the gap between education and the real-world hospitality industry, the academy provides selected youth from the community with the opportunity to gain a recognised qualification, develop practical skills and experience the workings of a five-star hotel environment, at no cost to the participants.\n\nThe inaugural programme is a Tertiary and Vocational Education Commission-approved NVQ Level 03 \u2013 Hotel Operation Multitasker Programme, offering the participants a structured pathway into the hospitality industry and the opportunity to build a foundation for a long-term career.\n\nThe academy is based at The Eden Beruwala, BHR\u2019s flagship five-star property on Sri Lanka\u2019s Golden Mile, providing an ideal setting for the aspiring hospitality professionals to learn and grow. With a fully operational luxury hotel as their learning environment, the students gain exposure to the standards, service culture and day-to-day operations that define the hospitality industry.\n\nThe launch ceremony of the Learning Academy took place in the presence of BHR CEO Eksath Wijeratne, The Eden Beruwala and Thaala Bentota Cluster General Manager Rohan Gamage, Bentota Beruwala Hoteliers Association President Sibi Mathew, Kalutara Government Agent\u2019s Office Human Resource Officer Sampath Wasala and BHR Head of Learning and Development Kanishka Jayatunga, together with the members of the management team and the inaugural batch of students."
  },
