    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5ab40fcff195e426df37a23b564b0d6e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1773,
    "chunk_text": "Minister pledges to build Australia-like Sri Lanka\n\nIndustry and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunneththi has pledged to transform Sri Lanka into a country offering freedom, equality before the law and opportunities, similar to those available in Australia.\n\nAddressing the Sri Lankan Entrepreneurs\u2019 Night 2026 entrepreneur and investor conference in Melbourne, Handunneththi said the government was working to create a new economic environment that would provide greater opportunities for the citizens while attracting investors to Sri Lanka.\n\nThe conference, organised by the Australia Sri Lanka Business Forum on August 15, brought together more than 350 participants, including Australian and Sri Lankan entrepreneurs, investors, business leaders and politicians.\n\nHandunneththi said the government had been working over the past two years to establish a more investor-friendly, transparent and trustworthy economic environment, supported by measures aimed at strengthening good governance and controlling corruption.\n\nHe said Sri Lanka was also focusing on improving infrastructure to support economic growth and investment, including expanding port access, developing the highway network and modernising the country\u2019s transport sector through initiatives such as electric rail and metro bus systems. Handunneththi also highlighted large-scale renewable energy projects aimed at providing the businesses with energy at competitive prices, saying improved infrastructure and reliable energy supplies were essential for attracting investment.\n\nHe invited the Australian investors and entrepreneurs to participate in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic transformation, stressing that investment opportunities were available across sectors and at different scales."
