    "chunk_text": "Excluding the foreign-exchange gains, the underlying second-quarter profit after tax amounted to Rs.9.6 billion, up 76 percent from a year earlier and 4 percent from the preceding quarter, the company said.\n\nOn a quarter-on-quarter basis, the group revenue increased 2 percent, earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation rose 6 percent to Rs.25.7 billion and the net profit advanced 10 percent. For the first six months, the group revenue rose 9.3 percent to Rs.95.52 billion, while the profit attributable to the shareholders more than doubled to Rs.19.30 billion, from Rs.9.20 billion.\n\nThe group invested Rs.18.5 billion in digital infrastructure during the six-month period, largely on its accelerated 5G rollout, which expanded to more than 1,000 live sites. The operating free cash flow stood at Rs.18.4 billion.\n\nDialog\u2019s board approved a second interim dividend of 70 cents per share for 2026, bringing the year-to-date dividend to Rs.1.40 per share."
