    "chunk_text": "The gains outweighed a 16 percent increase in finance expenses to Rs.1.75 billion. The net finance costs rose to Rs.1.25 billion, from Rs.1.08 billion.\n\nProfit before tax climbed 74 percent to Rs.1.74 billion, while the income-tax charge rose at a slower 17 percent to Rs.699.7 million.\n\nAfter the finance costs and tax, the tourism segment\u2019s loss widened to Rs.1.27 billion, from Rs.447.8 million.\n\nMaritime and freight logistics emerged as the largest operating profit contributor. The external revenue increased 28 percent to Rs.4.61 billion, while the operating profit rose 56 percent to Rs.1.26 billion. Profit after tax from the segment climbed 68 percent to Rs.1.32 billion.\n\nStrategic investments recorded the sharpest improvement, with the operating profit rising to Rs.836.1 million, from Rs.20.1 million. The segment posted a profit after tax of Rs.568.2 million, reversing a loss of Rs.161.9 million a year earlier, despite the external revenue growing by only 3.1 percent to Rs.2.31 billion.\n\nThe services segment\u2019s profit after tax increased 90 percent to Rs.425.9 million, helped by higher earnings from the equity-accounted investees. Its operating profit, however, declined 35 percent to Rs.111.5 million.\n\nThe improvement in the reported profit did not translate into stronger cash generation. The net cash used in the operating activities widened to Rs.2.54 billion, from Rs.1.16 billion, as the higher interest and tax payments compounded the working-capital outflows.\n\nTotal assets rose 1.8 percent from end-March to Rs.231.76 billion, while total equity increased 2 percent to Rs.106.37 billion.\n\nThe interest-bearing borrowings, including the bank overdrafts and other short-term facilities, increased to Rs.67.25 billion, from Rs.64.34 billion at end-March."
