    "chunk_text": "Global diesel price hike still a matter of concern for CPC\n\nColombo, Aug. 18 (Daily Mirror) - The continuous rise of diesel is still a matter of concern for Sri Lanka, an official said yesterday.\n\nThe average price of diesel around the world is 1.56 U.S. Dollar per litre. Chairman of the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation (CPC) D.J. Rajakaruna told Daily Mirror that diesel prices had been rising faster than crude oil benchmarks. He said that Sri Lanka imports a certain amount of diesel in addition to refining crude oil for the purpose. Diesel is heavily used in transportation, power generation and farming activities.\n\nHe said that it would be challenging at the next price revision.\n\n\u201cWe can manage petrol prices. Still, petrol prices have not come down,\u201d he said.\n\nThe state of the global diesel market is getting even more precarious as the Russia-Ukraine war and the Iran crisis squeeze supply from multiple angles.\n\nRussian oil firms enter Sri Lanka fuel supply race as CPC opens refinery tenders\n\nOil market alarming for  Sri Lanka, CPC seeks meeting with President"
