    "md5": "cfccd9db3164c11032cab37bdc24c685",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 671,
    "chunk_text": "Dinesh Chandimal suffers injury, taken to hospital\n\nColombo, Aug. 18 (Daily Mirror) - Dinesh Chandimal had to leave the field after sustaining an injury to his right shoulder and neck during the first session of Day 4 of the first Test against India.\n\nThe incident occurred at the end of the fourth over when Chandimal dived and landed awkwardly while attempting to save a boundary.\n\nThe 36-year-old appeared to be in immediate discomfort, clutching his neck while remaining on the ground.\n\nA statement from Sri Lanka Cricket (SLC) confirmed that he was assessed by the team physiotherapist and doctor on the field before being taken to hospital for a precautionary scan."
