    "chunk_size_bytes": 1279,
    "chunk_text": "The Government is trying to recover the economy and improve living conditions within a capitalist framework. That is fundamentally different from running a socialist system.\n\nQ: The JVP originally promoted equality and non-discrimination. Do you think it has taken a different approach now and overlooked communal issues?\n\nBut equality means equal rights for all citizens, including equal language rights and protection from discrimination based on religion or other factors.\n\nThe Constitution recognises Sinhala and Tamil as official languages, but Government communication is still not consistently available in both languages. I have complained about this for decades under different Governments.\n\nThe present Government should address this. Ensuring equal language rights through the administrative system would be far cheaper than allowing grievances to accumulate and eventually contribute to conflict.\n\nI do not think the Government is deliberately refusing to implement the policy. It may simply lack an effective mechanism to do so. There should be strict requirements for all Government departments and agencies to implement the language policy, with consequences for failure.\n\nSri Lanka cannot build a genuinely equal society without addressing these practical issues."
