    "chunk_size_bytes": 723,
    "chunk_text": "BASL takes 22nd amendment battle to Supreme Court\n\nColombo, Aug. 18 (Daily Mirror) - The Bar Association of Sri Lanka (BASL) has filed a Special Determination petition before the Supreme Court challenging the constitutionality of the Bill titled \u201cTwenty-Second Amendment to the Constitution,\u201d which proposes to increase the retirement age of Supreme Court judges to 67 and Court of Appeal judges to 65.\n\nThe Bill was published as a Gazette Supplement dated August 7, 2026, and subsequently tabled in Parliament. It was presented by the Minister of Justice and National Integration.\n\nThe BASL is seeking a declaration that the Bill requires approval by the people at a referendum and a two-thirds majority in Parliament."
  },
