    "chunk_size_bytes": 1634,
    "chunk_text": "Warm weather advisory for Eastern Province, seven districts\n\nColombo, Aug. 18 (Daily Mirror) - The Meteorology Department has issued a Warm Weather Advisory for Wednesday (19), warning that the heat index could reach the \u2018Caution\u2019 level in parts of the Eastern Province and seven districts.\n\nThe advisory, issued by the Natural Hazards Early Warning Centre at 4.00 p.m. today (18), covers the Eastern Province and the districts of Jaffna, Kilinochchi, Vavuniya, Mullaitivu, Polonnaruwa and Monaragala.\n\nAccording to the Department, the heat index\u2014the temperature felt by the human body\u2014is expected to increase to the \u2018Caution\u2019 level in some areas during the daytime.\n\nThe heat index is calculated using relative humidity and maximum temperature and does not represent the actual maximum air temperature.\n\nThe Department urged people to take precautions, including staying hydrated, limiting strenuous outdoor activities and taking frequent breaks in shaded areas.\n\nPeople working outdoors were advised to wear lightweight, white or light-coloured clothing, while the public was urged to check on elderly and sick persons. Motorists were also warned never to leave children unattended inside vehicles.\n\nUnder the heat index scale, temperatures of 39\u201345\u00b0C are considered the \u2018Caution\u2019 level, at which prolonged exposure and activity may cause fatigue and continued activity could lead to heat cramps.\n\nThe advisory was issued in consultation with health authorities, and the public was also advised to follow any additional guidance issued by the Disaster Preparedness and Response Division of the Ministry of Health."
  },
