    "chunk_text": "The Parliamentary Caucus also indicated that relevant young people could be invited to engage with appropriate parliamentary committees, creating a pathway through which young people\u2019s knowledge, experiences and proposals can contribute to parliamentary deliberations beyond the dialogue itself.\n\nThis mechanism is intended to ensure that the issues raised during the dialogue are documented and can continue to be followed up through the relevant parliamentary processes.\n\nThe Gampaha engagement forms part of the first phase of a broader Voice to Policy Dialogue series covering Gampaha, Kandy and Batticaloa.\n\nEach dialogue will follow the same participatory model, giving young people an opportunity to identify and prioritise issues relevant to their communities before engaging directly with Members of Parliament.\n\nThe initiative is intended to create a stronger connection between young people\u2019s lived experiences and parliamentary policymaking, while allowing Parliament to hear perspectives from young people across different districts and communities.\n\nThe Parliamentary Caucus for Open Parliament Initiative and the Coalition for Inclusive Impact (CII) are working together to create these spaces for meaningful youth\u2013Parliament engagement, with the first phase providing a foundation for expanding the dialogue to additional districts in the future.\n\nThe Voice to Policy Dialogue represents a practical step towards a more participatory relationship between young citizens and Parliament \u2014 creating opportunities for young people not only to voice their concerns, but to contribute ideas, propose solutions and engage with the parliamentary processes through which public policy is shaped."
