    "md5": "897d7dd3bf5ecd6f360346169f87fbd8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 824,
    "chunk_text": "22 illegal structures demolished along Ahangama beach strip\n\nColombo, Aug. 19 (Daily Mirror) - Authorities demolished at least 22 unauthorized structures, including several beachside restaurants and caf\u00e9s, along the Ahangama beach strip yesterday.\n\nPolice said the demolitions were carried out by the Department of Coast Conservation and Coastal Resource Management in accordance with legal procedures.\n\nThe department previously identified more than 2,500 illegal constructions across Sri Lanka\u2019s coastal zone.\n\nDirector General of the Department of Coast Conservation and Coastal Resource Management, Dr. Terney Pradeep Kumara, said the process of removing unauthorized structures had already commenced.\n\nUnder existing regulations, construction is prohibited within a zone extending 10 to 25 metres from the shoreline."
  },
