    "md5": "269a5774c9baedca39e2867d08dca4a5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1868,
    "chunk_text": "Accor debuts Pullman brand in Sri Lanka with two hotels\n\nFron left: Kedar Dighe - General Manager, Pullman Colombo City Centre; Dilan Christostom - Director \u2013 Finance and Corporate Planning, Softlogic Holdings PLC;\u00a0 Sid Solanki Sid Solanki \u2013 CEO - Leisure Sector and Group Asset Management Softlogic Retail Holdings (Pvt) Ltd; Ashok Pathirage - Chairman and Managing Director of the Softlogic Group and Softlogic Holdings PLC; Ranju Alex - Chief Executive Officer, Accor South Asia; Vineet Mishra - Vice President , Premium Midscale Economy, Accor South Asia; Balvinder Sahrawat - Vice President Developments, Accor South Asia; Anil Chavan- General Manager, Pullman Bentota Resort and Spa\n\nFrench hospitality group Accor has introduced its Pullman brand to Sri Lanka through two properties in Colombo and Bentota, expanding its premium hotel portfolio in South Asia.\n\nThe Pullman Colombo City Centre and Pullman Bentota Resort & Spa have opened in partnership with Softlogic Holdings PLC, adding a combined 384 rooms to the brand\u2019s regional network.\n\nPullman Colombo City Centre features 219 rooms and suites, alongside restaurants and bars, meeting and event facilities, a rooftop infinity pool, spa and fitness centre. The hotel is positioned to serve business, leisure and meetings-related demand in the capital.\n\nThe Bentota resort, located between the Bentota River and the Indian Ocean, comprises 165 rooms, family rooms and suites. Its facilities include restaurants, water sports and wellness offerings, as well as venues for meetings, weddings and other events.\n\nFinancial details of the partnership and the investment associated with the two properties were not disclosed.\n\nAccor South Asia CEO Ranju Alex said Sri Lanka represented an important growth market for the hotel group, supported by demand across business, leisure and experiential tourism."
  },
