    "chunk_text": "Lethargic institutions vs. Right to Information letters\n\nLocal governments -- there are some 325 municipalities, urban councils, Pradeshiya sabhas & 9 Provincial Councils spending around Rs. 6 billion in 2026. There are many SLAS officers at 6 different levels, for\u00a0 e.g. Secretary,\u00a0 Commissioner,\u00a0 Deputies & Assistants in many departments. Yet,\u00a0 very poor performance is very poor when it comes to serving the community.\n\nThe office telephone exchanges do not answer calls, letters to them are not acknowledged & left with clerks\u00a0 (management assistants). Governors are missing in the organisation charts. The Regional & Local Government Division of the Public Service Ministry in Colombo exercises no authority over the provincial administration. Many functions accepted as delegated can be shared with that ministry if it has initiative.\n\nKeep on sending\u00a0 Right to Information letters & ask why to make them RTIs.\u00a0 Address to Local Government\u00a0 Secretary or department head as Information Officer -- acknowledgement is due within 7 working days after its receipt. The reply is due 14 working days thereafter. Send weekly reminders. Thereafter write Appeal letter to LG Secretary as Designated Officer. If there is no acknowledgement after 7 days,\u00a0 warn the default will be reported to RTI Commission. Inform your council/sabha member (after their election). Also, people can fForm non-political Rate Payers Associations."
