    "md5": "012f0341d6401d7bf7ec814976bf0bb5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1206,
    "chunk_text": "Second, our northern sea border requires permanent, modern surveillance infrastructure. The historical legacy of the northern smuggling corridor cannot be erased overnight. Providing the Sri Lanka Navy and Coast Guard with advanced radar technology, aerial drones, and joint patrol agreements with Indian maritime authorities is essential.\n\nFinally, community awareness and public trust must be rebuilt across vulnerable neighborhoods. Local youth in low-income urban areas are often lured into becoming mules or dealers out of economic desperation. State intelligence agencies must engage deeply with community leaders, schools, and local organisations to spot early warning signs and protect young people from predatory gangs. At the same time, supply-side eradication must be paired with compassionate, accessible rehabilitation facilities for the thousands of young Sri Lankans jailed due to\u00a0 drug addiction. President Dissanayake has proven that strong political leadership combined with decisive police work can overcome international borders. Maintaining this uncompromising standard will determine whether this moment is remembered as a short-lived crackdown or a permanent victory for the nation."
  },
