    "chunk_size_bytes": 1922,
    "chunk_text": "Inside Sri Lanka\u2019s strategic blueprint for global tourism marketing promotion\n\nFor more than a decade, Sri Lanka\u2019s hospitality and tourism sector navigated one of the most turbulent operating environments in modern travel history without a unified, sustained global brand campaign. From unprecedented macroeconomic realignments to the lingering aftereffects of global disruption, the island\u2019s tourism trade relied heavily on private sector resilience, organic word-of-mouth, and tactical crisis management.\n\nYesterday, that decade-long promotional void officially came to an end. Gathered before an audience of hoteliers, inbound tour operators, airline executives, and international media, the Ministry of Tourism and the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau (SLTPB) unveiled a comprehensive, two-stage promotional offensive. Anchored under the thematic identity that Sri Lanka has more to say, with the global declaration that the world is listening, the initiative marks a decisive transition from reactive crisis marketing to a structured, data-driven promotional architecture.\n\nDetailed by SLTPB Chairman Buddhika Hewawasam, the blueprint establishes an immediate Rs. 1.5 billion interim digital and public relations campaign running from August 2026 through April 2027 across six primary source markets, followed by an expansive, multi-year Rs. 5 billion global branding campaign scheduled to roll out in March 2027 and run through February 2029.\n\n\u201cThis is not just promises made in the air; it is very much solid, very much structured, very much planned,\u201d Hewawasam said while Deputy Minister of Tourism Prof. Ruwan Ranasinghe reinforced the milestone, noting that \u201cthis has been a day that all were waiting for years.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhenever we sit for a press conference, the question that is asked is, \u2018Where is the global campaign?\u2019 So it is right here now, and we are launching it here today,\u201d he said."
