    "chunk_text": "Looking ahead, the launch of the subsequent global campaign is designed to propel arrivals past the 3 million mark in 2027, yielding over 5 billion US dollars in earnings. Ultimately, this framework builds toward a long-term vision of 5 million arrivals and an annual revenue contribution of 8 billion to 10 billion US dollars by 2030. The core objective, however, extends far beyond headline volume. The primary structural challenge confronting the industry has long been the imbalance between volume and yield. As articulated during the launch, the central priority is attracting quality, high-spending visitors whose daily expenditure and dwell time reflect the true value of the island\u2019s offering, shifting the marketing narrative away from generic destination postcards toward high-yield, experiential engagements.\n\nBy addressing these four pillars, the state promotional apparatus aims to dismantle seasonal limitations that have traditionally created sharp peaks and troughs in tourist arrivals. While the southern and western coastlines experience monsoon conditions during specific months, the eastern shores provide nine consecutive months of calm seas and favorable marine conditions, a geographic asset that has historically suffered from inadequate international promotion.\n\nRather than presenting static historical landmarks or generic landscapes, the creative direction of the campaign pivots entirely around immersive human experiences. Under the concept of seven experiences within one island, the presentation mapped out how distinct pillars align directly with global travel demand."
