    "chunk_text": "Rather than presenting static historical landmarks or generic landscapes, the creative direction of the campaign pivots entirely around immersive human experiences. Under the concept of seven experiences within one island, the presentation mapped out how distinct pillars align directly with global travel demand.\n\nThis creative campaign device is structured to highlight more of culture, flavor, and wildlife, alongside more of delight, connection, and nature, echoing the message that Sri Lanka has more to say. Each pillar is dynamically tailored to source markets, ensuring that Western European campaigns emphasize wellness, nature, and heritage, while campaigns in India and East Asia highlight MICE, destination weddings, and luxury leisure. Unexplored destinations such as Dunhinda, Panama, the Knuckles Mountain Range, and pristine northern locations like Kilinochchi are brought to the forefront to deliver authentic, uncrowded travel experiences.\n\nThe execution timeline presented by the SLTPB has been structured to maintain year-round international engagement, avoiding the fragmented, short-burst advertising attempts of the past. The Rs. 1.5 billion interim phase focuses on six primary source markets, beginning immediately in Australia with a six-month digital blitz and public relations campaign running from August 2026 to February 2027."
