    "chunk_text": "To demonstrate the quantitative rigor underpinning the campaign, the presentation highlighted the specific key performance indicators established for the phase one Australia activation. The projected volume and engagement scope target 16 million to 18 million total ad impressions across all channels. The campaign aims for a combined reach of 5 million to 8 million individuals across YouTube, Meta, and TikTok, alongside driving 125,000 to 205,000 web traffic clicks directly to the campaign microsite and securing 4 million to 5 million full video content views. These performance benchmarks establish an operational discipline where every promotional rupee is tied directly to measurable reach, engagement, and referral traffic into destination booking platforms.\n\n\u201cTHASL is the biggest investor in Sri Lanka tourism. Over the last several decades, we have invested more than 15 billion US dollars,\u201d Hettigoda stated, noting that member properties span from Jaffna in the north to Dondra Point in the south, ranging from five-room boutique villas to 500-room resorts. Reflecting on the industry\u2019s decade-long wait for a state-led global campaign, he highlighted the fiduciary stakes involved: \u201cToday you have embarked on a dream that we have had for the last 10 years. This dream has been so elusive that sometimes I think you were ignoring our questions or sometimes not meeting us. Honorable Deputy Minister, sometimes we call the Chairman, he is in the office, but he doesn\u2019t come to the phone because he knows exactly what question we are going to ask him! Because as investors, we are responsible for the shareholders to give a return, and that return can only come if the pillars that you mentioned, high-spending tourists, long-stay tourists, are met.\u201d\n\nHettigoda warned against post-launch complacency, urging authorities to adopt a culture of daily optimization rather than resting on promotional announcements."
  },
