    "chunk_text": "\u201cIn the next season, we will have about five new airlines coming into Sri Lanka. We have already, I think started yesterday, we have VietJet, Thai Airways, French Bee, Jetstar, and of course British Airways will start their operations to Sri Lanka,\u201d he noted, urging the state to implement joint promotional mechanisms that support seat capacity and encourage airlines to increase flight frequencies. Bilateral strategic marketing pacts have already been executed with Emirates, with discussions underway to finalize agreements with IndiGo, Turkish Airlines, and Qatar Airways. Simultaneously, Jayasundera emphasized that reaching 5 million arrivals and generating 8 billion to 10 billion US dollars in revenue by 2030 requires unlocking domestic air travel to seamlessly connect coastal resorts with cultural and eastern aerodromes, transforming Sri Lanka into a true year-round destination.\n\nTo ensure accountability, the Market Development Facility, funded by the Australian Government, is providing local agency oversight, training, and independent campaign monitoring and evaluation systems. Furthermore, the Digital Marketing Association of Sri Lanka is assisting with campaign optimization frameworks and staff training, building on the digital momentum established during the DICTA initiative.\n\nThe campaign is also engineered to future-proof Sri Lanka\u2019s search presence as travelers increasingly rely on artificial intelligence assistants, generative chatbots, and short-form video algorithms to plan travel. Hewawasam explained that destination data and regional itineraries are being optimized so that AI platforms accurately index Sri Lanka\u2019s offerings."
