    "chunk_size_bytes": 1757,
    "chunk_text": "Dr. Nandalal Weerasinghe, Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s improving credit profile and the potential for further upgrades, \u201cThe IMF views Sri Lanka as a case study of a country that has achieved a relatively rapid recovery. With all three major international rating agencies currently rating Sri Lanka at CCC, there is a clear pathway towards an upgrade to B-, a level comparable to where we stood before the crisis. This reflects the improving confidence in Sri Lanka. Investors who wait for the ratings upgrade may find that the market has already priced in the improvement. The opportunity to invest is now\u201d.\n\nThe broader regional investment potential of Sri Lanka was highlighted by Dr. Naveen Gunawardane, Co-Founder and Managing Director of Lynear Wealth Management, \u201cA play on srilanka is not a play on a single country play it is really a play on South Asia\u2019s growth and South Asia is going to be a key driver of growth in the global economy over the next 5 to 10 years\u201d.\n\nThe forum also highlighted the opportunities available through Port City Colombo, particularly for international investors seeking greater flexibility in capital flows and access to overseas markets. Thulci Aluwihare, Deputy Managing Director of CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt) Ltd, highlighted these opportunities, \u201cYou can invest in Australian dollars in Port City Colombo. Some of the restrictive repatriation and capital account rules that apply across South Asia do not apply in the Port City. The capital account is more relaxed because you are bringing your business capital from overseas, and your source markets and revenues are also overseas. That creates a much more flexible environment for international investors.\u201d"
