    "chunk_text": "\u201cOur performance during the first half of 2026 reflects the continued success of our business model,\u201d Managing Director and CEO Mohamed Azmeer said in the earnings commentary.\n\nross the retail, small and medium-sized enterprise and corporate segments while maintaining the asset quality.\n\nThe gross stage three financing ratio was unchanged at 2.8 percent, while the net ratio improved to 1.1 percent, from 1.2 percent.\n\nThe bank\u2019s total capital ratio declined to 13.8 percent, from 14.7 percent at end-2025, narrowing its buffer over the 12.5 percent regulatory minimum. Its common equity Tier 1 capital ratio fell to 12.4 percent, from 13 percent.\n\nFor the six months through June, the net profit increased 25 percent to Rs.1.12 billion, while the pre-tax profit rose 22 percent to Rs.1.87 billion."
