    "md5": "c05b89890ef0de08c11d26d4b970209c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1026,
    "chunk_text": "No details were provided on how the producers would be financed to invest in technology and packaging or how the government planned to connect them with the overseas buyers.\n\nThe minister also did not specify whether the strategy would include tax concessions, subsidised credit, grants or targeted support for the\u00a0priority industries.\n\nThe EDB said a significant number of issues raised by the exporters had been referred to the relevant state institutions through the Export Facilitation Task Force. The outstanding matters were discussed at yesterday\u2019s forum, although neither the issues nor the solutions agreed upon were disclosed.\n\nWijesinghe said the public and private sectors were working together under the National Export Development Plan to address the practical and trade-related constraints.\n\nHadunnetti said the government intended to simplify the policy decisions and create a more favourable operating environment for the exporters. An implementation timetable for the proposed changes is yet to be shared."
