    "md5": "5bfb16972dae47cd6a72c5267fa26b30",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1558,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThis has been a day that all of us were waiting for years,\u201d Prof. Ranasinghe noted.\n\n\u201cWhenever we sit for a press conference, the question that is asked is, \u2018Where is the global campaign?\u2019 So, it is right here now and we are launching it here today.\u201d\n\nThe industry stakeholders warmly welcomed the long-awaited campaign but stressed the need for strict accountability and collaborative execution.\n\nSri Lanka Association of Inbound Tour Operators President Nalin Jayasundera urged the authorities to establish joint promotional mechanisms with international tour operators and airlines, pointing out that stakeholder synergy is vital for achieving the ambitious five million arrival target by 2030.\n\n\u201cStarting with six important source markets is a strong step but I believe we should expand this to at least 10 countries without waiting for next year\u2019s global campaign, ensuring our top 10 source markets are actively addressed,\u201d Jayasundera said.\n\nMeanwhile, The Hotels Association of Sri Lanka President Ashoka Hettigoda highlighted that the hotel sector has invested over 15 billion dollars over the decades and requires sustained returns through high-spending, long-staying visitors.\n\nHettigoda proposed implementing monthly review briefings to track the campaign\u2019s empirical progress and ensure that every rupee spent yields the highest possible return on investment.\n\n\u201cExcellence is not a static award; it is a daily commitment to improve. Now that the campaign has been launched, we cannot afford complacency,\u201d Hettigoda said."
  },
