    "language": "en",
    "md5": "38f252c42426744bfd7fb06e9db49214",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1906,
    "chunk_text": "I want to raise one question. What is the country which was successful by using this IMF programme or the IMF conditions? Look and countries like Greece and Argentina. Even the other countries where IMF programme was implemented it was a failure. In one hand, we have that reality, because this is not the first time, it\u2019s the 17th time.\n\nAccording to the Central Bank Governor we are short of dollars, and according to his explanation 8.2 billion US dollars is enough to pay debts. We are not going to gain that within a few months.\n\nThis is the way we put forward our programme; with the support of the masses. And we are going to impose new taxes, not for the masses, but for the some of the capitalists, because they have enough wealth and at the same time they have enough profit as well. We are going to introduce new taxes for the top capitalists and release the vat and the other taxes imposed on the masses. We will continue to fight against these IMF measures. That is one of the major components of our programme.\n\nQ\u00a0Does this mean you\u2019re encouraging a participatory governance system. Is that what you\u2019re saying?\n\nYes, we are very open to say that our ultimate goal is socialism. There\u2019s no difference. We need to go through a transition period. But how do we go through this period? By getting support of the masses.\n\nEven though we come to power, we should maintain some organization amongst the masses, with the workers trade unions, peasants and everybody. So they are members. In a participatory democracy, people have a voice on a regular basis, not after five years or after election by election,\n\nQ\u00a0Don\u2019t you think that itself could create a monopoly where capitalists will get together and they will find a way to oppress the rest of the masses? When you try to impose tax on these people, don\u2019t you think that the downtrodden masses who work under them will be affected?"
  },
  {
