    "chunk_text": "Market breadth remained negative, with 93 securities advancing against 121 decliners, resulting in an advance-to-decline ratio of 0.77. The weaker breadth indicated that selling pressure remained broader than the relatively small declines in the headline indices suggested.\n\nSAMP.N remained the largest negative contributor, reducing the ASPI by 17.68 points. BREW.N, BUKI.N, JKH.N and CDB.N also weighed on the index.\n\nAmong notable trades, SEYB.N recorded the highest individual counter turnover at approximately LKR 153.18 million, followed by HNB.X with LKR 95.38 million and JKH.N with LKR 93.70 million.\n\nOverall, the session reflected continued consolidation at the CSE, with the ASPI recording its third consecutive decline. However, the relatively modest index losses compared with the broader negative market breadth suggest that selected heavyweight counters continued to provide some support, helping the ASPI remain above the 21,400 level."
