    "chunk_text": "Veteran singer Nanda Malini dies at 82\n\nColombo, Aug. 20 (Daily Mirror) - Veteran Sri Lankan vocalist and one of the country\u2019s most celebrated singers, Nanda Malini, has passed away at the age of 82.\n\nSri Lanka Singers Association (SLSA) President Keerthi Pasquel, who said that arrangements for her final rites will be announced later.\n\nNanda Malini was widely regarded as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s greatest vocalists, with a career spanning several decades. Her powerful voice and distinctive style made her a beloved figure in Sinhala music.\n\nHer contribution to Sri Lankan music, particularly Sinhala film and classical music, has left a lasting legacy."
