    "language": "en",
    "md5": "2189622c2a88b4706608cacc118ed7ef",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1986,
    "chunk_text": "As the US\u2011Iran war continues and the 60\u2011day Memorandum of Understanding that saw more clashes than talks expired on Monday amid a widening trust deficit between the parties, the two countries seem more determined to exhaust each other in a war of attrition than to strike a deal to end the conflict.\n\nIn a Truth Social post, US President Donald Trump described his new salvo \u2014 with capital letters for emphasis \u2014 as the \u201cMOST CRUSHING ECONOMIC OPERATION EVER TAKEN AGAINST ANY COUNTRY\u201d.\n\n\u201cThis will be Economic Warfare and Isolation on an unprecedented scale. Their navy is gone, their air force is destroyed, their military factories are now rubble, their currency is worthless, and their country is hanging by a thread,\u201d he said.\n\nTrump warned that any country supporting Tehran in any way will face \u201cTREMENDOUS Economic Consequences,\u201d but did not mention a specific country or what actions Washington is expected to take. Analysts, however, said the warning is directed at China, which buys more than 80 percent of Iran\u2019s oil.\n\n\u201cThis will be an ECONOMIC D\u2011DAY, and we need all of our Allies to stand with the United States of America to isolate and defeat the Iran threat,\u201d Trump said. \u201cThese maniacs are on the ropes, and these HISTORIC MEASURES will cripple them and their ability to project terror worldwide. IRAN WILL NEVER HAVE A NUCLEAR WEAPON.\u201d\n\nIranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi yesterday dismissed Trump\u2019s newly announced sanctions as a diversion from domestic American issues, warning that the \u201cso-called \u2018Economic D-Day\u2019\u201d would only bring further defeat to Washington.\n\nIt appears that the US acted in coordination with the UAE. The Gulf state did not resort to economic warfare even as more than 1,000 Iranian missile and drone attacks hit the country in the early stages of the war, though it could have.\n\nIran yesterday denied firing missiles at the UAE, claiming it was a \u2018false flag operation\u2019 by Israel and the US."
  },
