    "description": "EO Sri Lanka begins new chapter under President Abeetha Perera",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/EO-Sri-Lanka-begins-new-chapter-under-President-Abeetha-Perera/34-796312",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1787272884.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-21-dailyftlk-4ec6dfe9-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ed765ccc84300b6a13d63863909c74c8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1576,
    "chunk_text": "EO Sri Lanka begins new chapter under President Abeetha Perera\n\nEO Sri Lanka President and Board of Directors (from left); President Abeetha Perera, Umayanga Nanayakkara, Imran Akbarally, Sujan Suresh, Tarusha Weerasooria, Shanika Arsecularatne, Shanjeeve Sriskandarajah, Humaid Khalid, Losini Gajendran, Divek Amrith, Chirath Devasurendra, Chathura Samarasinghe and Chamindra Gamage\n\nEO Sri Lanka officially welcomed the 2026\u201327 EO year on 1 July 2026 as the chapter ushered in a new era of leadership under President of W. A. Perera & Co. Ltd., (WAPCO) Director Abeetha Perera and his newly appointed Board of Directors.\n\nThe ceremonial handover saw the presidency baton passed from of Stafford Motor Company Executive Director Tarindra Kaluperuma, symbolising a seamless transition and the beginning of another exciting chapter for Sri Lanka\u2019s entrepreneurial community.\n\nHaving successfully led the chapter through a year Beyond Borders & Beyond Limits, Tarindra Kaluperuma concluded his tenure by entrusting the leadership of the chapter to Abeetha Perera, whose vision for the year is captured in the theme \u201cBeyond the Edge\u201d \u2014 an invitation to practice Conscious Leadership and turn it into Transformational Action.\n\nThe theme reflects a commitment to developing entrepreneurs who lead with intention, self-awareness, and purpose while inspiring meaningful transformation within their organisations and communities. It challenges members to think beyond conventional boundaries, embrace innovation, and pursue growth with courage, resilience, and authenticity."
  },
