    "md5": "d456f970ad4832935866bd8b48143c35",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1351,
    "chunk_text": "According to Rasamanickam, Dr. Jayatissa acknowledged the shortage and assured Parliament that steps were being taken to resolve the immediate problem within one week. The Minister also said a special medical team had been established to address the issue.\n\n\u201cA procurement delay must never become a patient\u2019s medical crisis,\u201d Rasamanickam said.\n\nHe said he had also received information that similar difficulties could be affecting Government hospitals in the Northern and Eastern Provinces, including Jaffna, and called for urgent verification.\n\nRasamanickam urged the Health Ministry to continuously monitor Filgrastim stocks and requirements at every major Government hospital, including available quantities, requirements and the number of days existing stocks would last.\n\n\u201cI welcome the Minister\u2019s assurance that the immediate shortage will be addressed within one week. However, this cannot end with a temporary solution. \u201cThe Ministry of Health must establish a reliable long-term procurement and supply mechanism for Filgrastim and other essential cancer medicines so that the same crisis does not recur,\u201d he said.\n\n\u201cThe Government has a fundamental responsibility to ensure that no cancer patient is forced to delay or discontinue treatment because an essential medicine is unavailable or unaffordable,\u201d Rasamanickam added."
