    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d9acc1456db7e99bb21e43de8b0d2998",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1903,
    "chunk_text": "People\u2019s Leasing Company among Top 100 most valuable brands\n\nFrom left: People\u2019s Leasing CEO and GM Sanjeewa Bandaranayake, Brand Finance Chairman Ruchi Gunewardena and Echelon Media Co-Founder and Executive Director Antoinette Ludowyk\n\nPeople\u2019s Leasing & Finance PLC (PLC) has been recognised among the top 100 most valuable brands in the Brand Finance Sri Lanka Top 100 Most Valuable Brands 2026 ranking.\n\nFurthermore, it is noteworthy that the company has secured a position among the top three most valuable brands within the non-bank financial institution sector.\n\nBrand Finance publishes the annual ranking of the world\u2019s most valuable brands across various countries.\n\nHeadquartered in London, Brand Finance is one of the world\u2019s leading independent brand valuation and strategy consultancy firms. Through its globally recognised brand valuation methodology, Brand Finance evaluates the financial values and strength of brands. According to the Brand Finance brand valuation rankings, PLC has recorded significant growth in its brand value this year. According to the Brand Finance brand rankings, PLC has advanced three positions, moving up from the 25th position in 2025 to the 22nd position in 2026.\u00a0 Furthermore, the company\u2019s brand value has increased from Rs.5.4 billion to Rs.7.5 billion, while also achieving an AA+ brand strength rating. This reflects an important milestone for the company, demonstrating its strong brand image, customer trust and outstanding performance in the financial services sector.\n\nPLC extends its sincere gratitude to its loyal customers and dedicated employees for contributing to this achievement.\n\nThe company remains committed to strengthening its services by continuing to provide innovative and reliable financial solutions, maintaining its leadership position in Sri Lanka\u2019s financial sector and delivering greater value to its customers."
  },
