    "chunk_text": "Another key measure discussed was the introduction of rapid test kits capable of detecting chemical residues in fruits within a short period. Officials were instructed to identify suitable testing kits and take steps to procure them to facilitate the testing of fruits entering the market.\n\nSeveral measures were identified during the meeting, including the introduction of a special certification for traders who comply with SLS 1767 and Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP) standards and do not use toxic chemicals. Consumers would then be encouraged to purchase fruits from certified outlets.\n\nPlans were also discussed to establish standards for safe fruit-ripening chambers using ethylene gas and provide technical assistance to small and medium-scale traders.\n\nTraining programmes will be conducted in collaboration with institutions such as HARTI, ITI and SLSI to educate traders on safe fruit-ripening methods and the proper identification of ripe fruits."
