    "chunk_text": "Buying sentiment persists in long-end maturities\n\nThe mixed sentiment persisted in the secondary market yesterday, with moderate volumes and market activity.\n\nAmong the executed trades, 2030 segment saw some profit taking with 01.03.2030, 01.08.2030 and 15.10.2030 traded between 10.75% - 10.90%.\n\nOn the other hand, 01.02.2031 maturity saw buying interest, trading at 10.95%. Moving ahead, 01.10.2032 changed hands at 11.20%. Moreover, 15.01.2033 and 01.11.2033 traded in the range of 11.53% - 11.35% and 01.08.2036 and 01.07.2037 traded between 12.10% - 12.00%.\n\nOn the external front, the LKR marginally appreciated against the USD, standing at Rs. 331.23/USD, compared to Rs. 331.83/USD seen earlier. Market liquidity in the banking system expanded to Rs. 300.25bn from Rs. 288.98bn recorded previously.\n\nPopular maturities: 01.03.2030:+18bps, 01.08.2030: +3bps, 15.10.2030: -6bps, 01.11.2033: -6bps, 01.07.2037: -4bps"
