    "language": "en",
    "md5": "2618f6ed8e701729bce6b37f67357a7e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1837,
    "chunk_text": "As a result, operating profit grew at a slower 22 percent to Rs. 19.88 billion. Net finance costs eased 3 percent to Rs. 12.58 billion, helping profit before tax from continuing operations surge 78 percent to Rs. 7.58 billion. The tax charge more than doubled to Rs. 2.82 billion.\n\nFinancial services generated Rs. 64.18 billion in gross income, up from Rs. 48.57 billion a year earlier, but operating profit fell to Rs. 11.44 billion from Rs. 12.35 billion. The segment\u2019s profit before tax consequently declined to Rs. 11.44 billion from Rs. 12.35 billion.\n\nThe offset came from a substantial improvement in several other businesses. Manufacturing and trading narrowed its pre-tax loss to Rs. 1.27 billion from Rs. 2.09 billion, while leisure and real estate reduced its loss to Rs. 2.59 billion from Rs. 3.60 billion. Plantation and agriculture swung to a Rs. 316 million pre-tax loss from a Rs. 6 million profit a year earlier.\n\nThe Group\u2019s \u201cothers and eliminations\u201d category also improved sharply, recording a pre-tax loss of Rs. 191 million compared with a Rs. 3.56 billion loss in the corresponding quarter. Profit from equity-accounted investees fell to Rs. 277 million from Rs. 691 million.\n\nLOLC\u2019s balance sheet continued to expand. Total assets reached Rs. 2.46 trillion at end-June, up from Rs. 2.32 trillion at end-March and Rs. 2.10 trillion a year earlier. Advances and other loans increased to Rs. 1.05 trillion from Rs. 981.81 billion three months earlier, while deposit liabilities rose to Rs. 739.56 billion from Rs. 694.27 billion.\n\nThe expansion came with heavier funding and credit costs. Interest-bearing borrowings increased to Rs. 714.81 billion from Rs. 673.25 billion at end-March, while financial-services impairment charges rose to Rs. 8.51 billion from Rs. 5.22 billion in the year-earlier quarter."
  },
