    "chunk_text": "The deal was structured as a US$ 22.0 million acquisition of a 75 percent stake, funded partly through a US$ 16.1 million foreign-currency borrowing facility over three and a half years. Twiga reported revenue of US$ 38 million \u2014 approximately Rs. 12.6 billion at current exchange rates \u2014 at an 8 percent normalised EBITDA margin for FY2025. The transaction lifts Hemas\u2019s international revenue contribution from 3 to 10 percent of group turnover; group executives said the deal is expected to become earnings-accretive from FY2029.\n\nChandra reaffirmed that domestic investment remains the priority. \u201cOur more than 80 to 85 percent investment continues to be in Sri Lanka,\u201d he said. \u201cBecause that\u2019s where we believe is our home market, that\u2019s where we have a right to win. And once we perfect the product and the way to do that capabilities in Sri Lanka, only then we will take it out.\u201d US$ 100 million is available for possible acquisitions over the next three years, separate from a further US$100 million earmarked for hospital machinery upgrades \u2014 keeping the group primed to expand across consumer goods, healthcare and regional supply chains. (NF)"
