    "md5": "c872cde9b37efcdc2b16f62e1b7c6134",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 930,
    "chunk_text": "To further optimise capital allocation, the company is prioritizing infrastructure sharing with other operators. By engaging in active and passive network sharing for towers, fiber, and radio spectrum, the operator aims to reduce capital intensity and save valuable foreign exchange in collaboration with the Telecommunications Regulatory Commission.\n\nReassuring stakeholders about the company\u2019s strong financial footing, De Silva highlighted the stark contrast from the financial struggles the state-owned enterprise faced just two years ago.\n\n\u201cSLT Mobitel is not the struggling company it was two years ago. We are profitable. We are self-funding our growth. We have built dollar reserves to protect the country from currency shocks. We are expanding 4G, rolling out 5G intelligently, and building world-class data centers, all without begging for new foreign loans or asking the government for bailouts,\u201d De Silva stated."
