    "md5": "14e936e022f48d131efe321d5c31b4c7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 478,
    "chunk_text": "Poor engine condition caused Colombo-KKS train breakdown: Deputy Minister\n\nThe poor condition of the engine caused the breakdown of the Colombo-Kankesanthurai (KKS) train yesterday (20), Deputy Minister of Transport Prasanna Gunasena told Parliament.\n\nResponding to an oral question raised by MP Kavinda Jayawardena, Dr. Gunasena said most of the engines currently in service were in poor condition.\n\n\u201cOur intention is to repair both the engines and the carriages,\u201d he said."
