    "chunk_text": "The Minister stressed that the shortage was not caused by any delay on the part of either the Health Ministry or the supplier. He said the Medical Supplies Division (MSD) had placed the order for the 2026 requirement more than nine months in advance, in January 2025.\n\nResponding to a question as to whether the Ministry could allow the use of the drug despite the absence of labels, given the urgent needs of patients, the Minister said discussions were underway to determine whether this could be permitted based on recommendations from the College of Oncologists and the College of Haematologists.\n\nHe added that relabeling the rejected stock would take at least six weeks."
