    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan star emerges as Chopra\u2019s biggest threat\n\nAUG.21 (Mirror Sports) - Neeraj Chopra will face a reshuffled javelin field at the Lausanne Diamond League on Friday night, with Sri Lanka\u2019s Rumesh Tharanga Pathirage emerging as one of the leading challengers following Julian Weber\u2019s withdrawal.\n\nPathirage arrives in Lausanne in outstanding form after producing a huge 92.62m throw in Rome earlier this season, making him one of the few athletes in the field to have surpassed the 90m mark this year.\n\nChopra, a two-time Lausanne winner, enters the contest with a season\u2019s best of 85.83m and will be chasing another strong performance against a field that still includes several major names.\n\nAnderson Peters, Jakub Vadlejch, Keshorn Walcott and Marc Anthony Minichello are among the notable competitors set to line up alongside the Indian star.\n\nThe javelin final is scheduled to begin at 11:52 p.m. IST on Friday, with Pathirage\u2019s 90m-plus form adding further intrigue to Chopra\u2019s latest Diamond League appearance."
