    "md5": "43b95ad988193a5e2492256d5a190159",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2019,
    "chunk_text": "Neil Marine strengthens boat building capacity with new Dikovita yard\n\nNeil Marine Group has expanded its boatbuilding operations with a new\u00a0Rs. 50 million-plus manufacturing facility at Dikovita, Wattala, as the company seeks to increase production, create jobs and strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s position in the international boatbuilding market.\n\nThe new yard, approved by the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka, has been established on previously abandoned land belonging to the Ceylon Fishery Harbours Corporation.\n\nThe project represents a\u00a0 public-private partnership aimed at putting underutilised state assets to productive use while expanding private-sector manufacturing capacity.\n\nThe company described the facility as a new chapter in its manufacturing journey, with its broader ambition captured in the message: \u201cBuilt in Sri Lanka. Exported to the world.\u201d\n\nThe facility was recently opened with religious observances led by the Maha Sangha under the patronage of the Incumbent of Ratmalana Mallikaramaya, Ven. Pandita Ranasgalle Gnanaweera Thero.\n\nThe occasion also paid tribute to the late Neil Fernando, founder of Neil Marine Group, whose vision helped build the company into a recognised name in Sri Lanka\u2019s boatbuilding industry over more than five decades.\n\nThe Dikovita yard is expected to provide additional production capacity for Neil Marine and support the company\u2019s plans to expand its presence in export markets. The company said the investment would contribute to higher export earnings and generate new employment opportunities.\n\nOperations at the facility are headed by Officer-in-Charge Ajith Susantha and his team, under the leadership of Group Chairman Kumari Fernando, Group President Manel Fernando and CEO Shan Perera.\n\nDeputy Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources Minister Rathna Gamage, Industries\u2019 Ministry Boatbuilding Sector Chairman Indra Kaushal Rajapaksha, representatives of the Export Development Board and other Government and industry officials attended the opening."
  },
