    "chunk_text": "A third way for Sri Lanka \u2013 lifting the rural economy\n\nOne that lifts the economic strength, financial, health and education status of the rural sector in Sri Lanka through participation, decision making and ownership by the rural community\n\nThe Sri Lankan Government has launched a national movement and development program, Praja Shakthi (meaning \u201cCommunity Strength\u201d or \u201cCommunity Power\u201d) as its flagship policy and program for rural empowerment and eradicating rural poverty. This is a very worthwhile program, and it needs to be supported. However, the Government could consider its core goal as uplifting the economic strength of the rural sector rather than just uplifting local communities and eliminating poverty as such a renewed goal will make the entire project more meaningful and attuned to very specifically lifting the sectors GDP, and through that, the national GDP as outlined in this article"
