    "md5": "5dc773d8b8f732a7f7cf8005d3dd1181",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1495,
    "chunk_text": "Alpha Tours marks 50-year partnership with Korean Air\n\nFrom left: Alpha Tours Managing Director Priyantha Mendis, Western Province Governor and Presidential Special Envoy for Foreign Investment Hanif Yosoof, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Sri Lanka Miyon Lee, Hanjin Logistics President and CEO Sam Sug Noh, Finco Holdings Vice Chairman Priyanjith Weerasooria and Hanjin Logistics President and CMO Emily Lee Cho\n\nAlpha Tours, a member of Finco Holdings, marked a significant milestone in Sri Lanka\u2019s aviation and travel industry by celebrating 50 years as the general sales agent (GSA) for Korean Air, making it the airline\u2019s longest serving GSA across its global network.\n\nThe golden jubilee celebration was held at The Hilton Colombo, bringing together leaders from the aviation, diplomatic and business communities to commemorate five decades of partnership.\n\nThe event reflected the long-standing relationship between Alpha Tours and Korean Air, highlighting a partnership that has contributed to strengthening passenger and cargo connectivity between Sri Lanka and international markets over the past five decades.\n\nA special highlight of the evening was the presence of Hanjin Logistics Corporation President and Chief Marketing Officer Emily Lee Cho, the granddaughter of the late Cho Choong-hoon, the founder of Hanjin Group and Korean Air.\n\nHer participation underscored the historic significance of the occasion and the enduring relationship between the two organisations."
