    "md5": "420118810c3925e9717afd6b0c490217",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1987,
    "chunk_text": "WCIC PRATHIBHABHISHEKA \u2013 Women Entrepreneur Awards 2026 invites applications\n\nFrom left: WCIC WEA 26 Co-Chairperson Wathsala Wickramanayake, WCIC WEA 26 Co-Chairperson Nilani Senevirathne, AIA Sri Lanka Director HR Thushari Perea, WCIC Chairperson Gayani De Alwis, WCIC First Vice Chairperson Ramani Ponnambalam and WCIC Second Vice Chairperson Thusitha Kumarakulasigham\n\nPrestigious awards programme returns to recognise Sri Lanka\u2019s most outstanding women entrepreneurs\n\nThe Women\u2019s Chamber of Industry and Commerce (WCIC) has officially announced the launch of WCIC PRATHIBHABHISHEKA \u2013 Women Entrepreneur Awards 2026, inviting women entrepreneurs from across Sri Lanka and the SAARC region to apply for the country\u2019s most prestigious business recognition programme.\n\nBuilding on the success of recent editions, the awards continue to celebrate women who have demonstrated business excellence, resilience, innovation and leadership while making meaningful contributions to Sri Lanka\u2019s economic growth.\n\nSpeaking at the launch, WCIC Chairperson Gayani De Alwis said, \u201cWCIC Prathibhabhisheka has grown into the country\u2019s foremost platform dedicated to recognising women entrepreneurs who continue to transform industries, create employment and strengthen the national economy. As we launch the 2026 edition, we once again invite women entrepreneurs from every corner of Sri Lanka to showcase their journeys and inspire the next generation of business leaders. The success stories of our past winners demonstrate the impact this recognition creates for both entrepreneurs and their businesses.\u201d\n\nThe previous edition attracted over 100 applications representing businesses of every scale, with participants from all nine provinces. A total of 47 awards were presented, including Overall Awards, Category Awards, Provincial Awards and Special Recognition Awards, reaffirming the programme\u2019s position as Sri Lanka\u2019s national benchmark for recognising women in business."
  },
