    "chunk_text": "The previous edition attracted over 100 applications representing businesses of every scale, with participants from all nine provinces. A total of 47 awards were presented, including Overall Awards, Category Awards, Provincial Awards and Special Recognition Awards, reaffirming the programme\u2019s position as Sri Lanka\u2019s national benchmark for recognising women in business.\n\nApplications are now open under the Start-up, Micro, Small, Medium and Large business categories. In addition to category awards, the outstanding applicants will be considered for several prestigious special awards, culminating in the presentation of the coveted Woman Entrepreneur of the Year 2026 title.\n\nThe programme also continues its commitment to recognising entrepreneurship across the country through provincial recognition while providing a platform for women entrepreneurs from the SAARC region to compete under the international category.\n\nInterested applicants can download the application from www.wcicsl.lk in the language they prefer or request an application directly from the WCIC office. Completed applications, together with the required supporting documentation, should be submitted before the closing date, which will be announced shortly.\n\nWCIC Prathibhabhisheka is supported by AIA Insurance \u2013 Platinum Partner, DFCC Aloka \u2013 Diamond/Official Banking Partner, McLarens \u2013 Gold Partner, Hayleys PLC, Maliban, Unilever Arunella \u2013 Silver Partners and Imrpa Teas and Pidilite Bronze Partners.\n\nAs Sri Lanka\u2019s national chamber for women in business, the WCIC remains committed to empowering women entrepreneurs through advocacy, networking, capacity building and recognition, with Prathibhabhisheka continuing as its flagship initiative to celebrate women who are shaping the country\u2019s business landscape."
