    "md5": "469ef267bc8f75a2965d9e403a2fdd73",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 513,
    "chunk_text": "On a year-on-year basis, the food category nevertheless showed a clear acceleration, with inflation rising to 4.9 percent in July, from 3.3 percent in June. Non-food inflation eased only marginally to 9.2 percent, from 9.3 percent, leaving it substantially above food inflation.\n\nThe 12-month moving average inflation rate also increased to 3.5 percent in July, from 2.9 percent in June, reflecting the cumulative build-up in price pressures despite the relatively modest month-on-month increase recorded in July."
