    "chunk_text": "The Minister also said that advances in modern healthcare cannot be achieved by a single individual or professional group. Cooperation among specialist doctors, medical officers, nurses and other healthcare professionals is essential to achieve the best outcomes, he said.\n\nThe programme focused on modern medical technologies, emerging trends, the expansion and improvement of neurosurgical services in Sri Lanka and future challenges facing the field.\n\nNeurosurgeons Association of Sri Lanka President Dr. Nirukshan Jayaweera chaired the session, while University of Colombo Vice-Chancellor Prof. Indika Karunathilaka attended as the special guest. Neurosurgeon Dr. Sunil Perera of Asiri Surgical Hospital attended as the guest of honour and delivered special lectures on neurosurgical services.\n\nAssociation Secretary Dr. Saman Pushpakumara, former presidents of the association and members of the Neurosurgeons Association of Sri Lanka were also present."
