    "md5": "dc19e157b636ef622411235c13542d05",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1377,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe fact that you are standing here today as university students is a testament to your determination and strength.\n\nYour journey is an example to the younger generation, particularly those who become discouraged when faced with difficulties,\u201d she said.\n\nShe said the Government would continue to support students with disabilities and noted that a monthly allowance had been introduced for students with disabilities from low-income families.\n\nA pilot programme has also been launched to provide technical assistance to support the education of children with disabilities, she said.\n\n\u201cThis recognition is not the end of your journey. It is only the beginning of a bright journey.\n\nWhatever your physical limitations may be, do not place limits on your dreams. Continue to work with determination to achieve them,\u201d Prime Minister Amarasuriya said.\n\nShe assured the students that the Government and the people of the country would continue to support them in achieving their aspirations.\n\nSpeaker Jagath Wickramaratne, Northern Province Governor Nagalingam Vedanayagan, Fisheries Minister Ramalingam Chandrasekar, MP Sugath Wasantha de Silva, President\u2019s Senior Additional Secretary G.G.S.C. Roshan, Jaffna District Secretary M. Piradeepan, MPs, government officials, university vice-chancellors, students with disabilities and their parents were among those present."
