    "chunk_text": "Polonnaruwa records highest temperature at 37.2\u00b0C\n\nColombo, August 22 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Polonnaruwa recorded the highest temperature in Sri Lanka at 37.2\u00b0C today (22), according to temperature data released by the Department of Meteorology.\n\nSeveral areas in the dry zone and eastern regions also experienced high temperatures. Mullaitivu and Monaragala recorded 36.7\u00b0C, while Pottuvil reached 36.1\u00b0C. Trincomalee and Matale recorded temperatures of 36.0\u00b0C.\n\nOther temperatures recorded across the country included 35.7\u00b0C in Vavuniya, 33.7\u00b0C in Anuradhapura, 33.0\u00b0C in Jaffna, 31.4\u00b0C in Colombo and 29.6\u00b0C in Galle.\n\nMeanwhile, Nuwara Eliya recorded the lowest maximum temperature at 19.7\u00b0C. Bandarawela recorded 28.8\u00b0C, while Katugastota recorded 29.0\u00b0C.\n\nThe latest data indicates that the highest temperatures were mainly concentrated in the northern, north-central and eastern parts of the country."
