    "chunk_text": "Polonnaruwa, Pothuvil record 37.5\u00b0C as heat intensifies\n\nColombo, Aug. 23 (Daily Mirror) - Polonnaruwa and Pothuvil recorded the highest maximum temperature in the country today (23), with temperatures reaching 37.5\u00b0C, the Meteorology said.\n\nThe highest temperature of 37.5\u00b0C was recorded in both Polonnaruwa and Pothuvil.\n\nTrincomalee recorded 37.0\u00b0C, while Mullaitivu and Monaragala recorded 36.8\u00b0C each. Mattala also recorded a high temperature of 34.9\u00b0C.\n\nSeveral other areas experienced temperatures above 33\u00b0C, including Vavuniya (35.9\u00b0C), Batticaloa (33.5\u00b0C), Badulla (33.2\u00b0C), Anuradhapura (33.9\u00b0C), Maha Illuppallama (33.8\u00b0C) and Ratnapura (31.9\u00b0C).\n\nMeanwhile, Nuwara Eliya recorded the lowest temperature among the locations shown, at 19.5\u00b0C.\n\nThe figures highlight the continued heat affecting several parts of the country, particularly the North Central, Eastern and Monaragala areas."
