    "chunk_text": "But we should also allow this case to remind us of what still needs to change. A successful conviction after fifteen years is certainly a reason for gratitude. It should not, however, become something we accept as normal.\n\nAt CPF, we will continue to stand beside survivors for as long as they need us. But ultimately, victim advocacy cannot depend only on organisations like ours carrying the burden. Child protection has to be a responsibility shared and prioritised by the entire justice system.\n\nToday, we are grateful that this survivor finally received justice. Tomorrow, we must continue working towards a system where the next child does not have to wait fifteen years.\n\n(The author is an Attorney-at-Law and Founder Child Protection Force)"
