    "description": "PAQS 2026: Connecting  Sri Lanka\u2019s quantity surveying profession  to the region",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/PAQS-2026-Connecting-Sri-Lanka-s-quantity-surveying-profession-to-the-region/34-796436",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1787531109.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-24-dailyftlk-b3679c68-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5e894e0c884ad6158549acb385b88e9c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1743,
    "chunk_text": "Prof. Weddikkara: I would describe PAQS as a bridge that connects Quantity Surveying professionals across different countries. The building sector is becoming increasingly multinational, with projects, consultants, contractors, investors and technologies crossing national borders. PAQS gives professional institutions an opportunity to connect, share knowledge and experiences, learn from one another and collectively strengthen the profession across the region.\n\nSeneviratne: This is only the second time Sri Lanka is hosting the Congress, following the first in 2011. It gives us exposure to current industry practices, best practices and new technology tools being used in the industry. When people come and present their findings, that knowledge is shared, and it becomes a good learning curve for the present generation as well as the future generation of the profession.\n\nQ: The theme is \u2018Constructing the Evolution: Unleashing Human Intelligence\u2019. What does that mean for the profession?\n\nSeneviratne: AI tools are now being used across industries, and the conference will focus on how they can benefit Quantity Surveying, while also identifying the roles where human intelligence will remain the main focus. That is a very worthwhile discussion for the profession.\n\nProf. Weddikkara: Technology should support our profession, not define it. The experience, judgement, ethics and wisdom of a Quantity Surveyor remain fundamental to good professional practice. The Congress gives us an opportunity to embrace technological advancement while preserving and strengthening the human intelligence that sits at the heart of the profession.\n\nQ: How does Sri Lanka\u2019s participation in PAQS benefit professionals and the domestic industry?"
