    "chunk_text": "Commenting on the initiatives, Digital Economy Ministry Secretary Waruna Sri Dhanapala said, \u201cDigital technologies, interoperable data systems and advanced analytics are becoming fundamental to modern governance. The Fisheries and Plantation Sector DSSs demonstrate how Digital Public Infrastructure can strengthen evidence-based decision-making, improve institutional coordination and enhance service delivery across strategically important sectors. Through IDAT, we are supporting a Government-led approach that uses trusted data and digital systems to advance economic resilience, sustainability, inclusive development and Sri Lanka\u2019s broader digital transformation.\u201d\n\nConnect to Care Inclusive Digital Agriculture Transformation (IDAT) Program Project Director Major General (Retd.) Chandana Priyantha Arangalla said: \u201cOur responsibility as the Program Management Office was to support coordination across a complex institutional environment and help ensure that the Government\u2019s objectives remained central throughout delivery. The platforms are now owned by the institutions they were designed to serve. Their long-term value will come from continued Government leadership, trusted data and consistent use in everyday decision-making.\u201d\n\nThe Fisheries and Plantation Sector Decision Support Systems represent an important foundation for Sri Lanka\u2019s continued digital agriculture transformation. By connecting institutions around reliable information and shared national priorities, the program supports a transition from fragmented reporting to coordinated action, and from data collection to measurable public impact."
