    "md5": "3c08261f8bc46468f644af7cb4af16df",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1544,
    "chunk_text": "With preparations for the 2027 Budget underway, President Dissanayake stressed the need to maintain financial discipline and operate within prescribed expenditure limits. He instructed officials to complete planning for all projects by November so that implementation could begin on schedule next year.\n\nPresident Dissanayake instructed officials to increase the capacity of small and medium-sized tanks and accelerate rehabilitation during the limited period between the end of the Yala season and the start of the Maha season, taking into account anticipated developments in the El Nino situation. Officials were directed to prioritise the work using already allocated funds.\n\nThe meeting also reviewed plans to reorganise the school system. The President instructed officials to assess schools with fewer than 50 students individually, including their physical condition and relevant data, before deciding on consolidation. The Government would provide transport facilities or an allowance where necessary, according to the PMD.\n\nA shortage of technical officers across Provincial Councils was also discussed, with officials instructed to prepare an expedited program to recruit and train technical assistants.\n\nLabour Minister and Deputy Finance and Planning Minister Dr. Anil Jayantha Fernando, Secretary to the President Dr. Nandika Sanath Kumanayake, Treasury Secretary Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma, provincial Chief Secretaries and officials from the Finance Commission, Finance Ministry and Presidential Secretariat attended the meeting."
