    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "72090e186034dc44b01a7912cc40794e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1895,
    "chunk_text": "Gamma Interpharm enters Cambodia, expands Sri Lanka\u2019s pharmaceutical export footprint\n\nFrom left: Gamma Interpharm DGM \u2013 Marketing and International Trade Vidhira Gunasekara, GM \u2013 Marketing Niseni Hewamallika, Chairman Kalana Hewamallika, Director \u2013 Operations Sugi Sivayogarajan and Junior Executive \u2013 Export Posonya Rithmanthi\n\nGamma Interpharm Ltd., has commenced exports of Sri Lankan-manufactured pharmaceuticals to Cambodia, marking a key milestone in its six-decade journey and strengthening the country\u2019s pharmaceutical manufacturing presence in regional markets.\n\nThe company launched its first pharmaceutical exports to Cambodia on 14 August 2026 at its manufacturing facility, in the presence of stakeholders and employees. Gamma Interpharm said the development makes it the first truly Sri Lankan pharmaceutical manufacturing company to export pharmaceuticals to Cambodia.\n\nThe entry into Cambodia forms part of Gamma Interpharm\u2019s broader strategy to expand its international footprint and establish locally manufactured pharmaceutical products in overseas markets. With a heritage shaped by associations with Warner Lambert Inc. and Pfizer Inc., USA, Gamma Interpharm has evolved over six decades as a Sri Lankan pharmaceutical manufacturer, progressively strengthening its manufacturing, quality assurance and analytical capabilities.\n\nThe company said the latest export milestone was driven by the vision and leadership of Chairman Kalana Hewamallika, who has focused on creating opportunities for Sri Lankan-manufactured pharmaceuticals in international markets.\n\nThe company\u2019s management and employees have also played a key role in supporting its international expansion strategy. Gamma Interpharm is equipped with modern pharmaceutical manufacturing technology and advanced analytical capabilities, supported by a skilled workforce with international exposure."
  },
  {
