    "md5": "fa5317100253dd1f46e308915e6b8be2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1886,
    "chunk_text": "VFS Global launches Republic of Korea visa services in Sri Lanka\n\nRepublic of Korea to Sri Lanka and Maldives Former Ambassador Miyon Lee (second from left), Embassy of the Republic of Korea Third Secretary and Consul Jung Haesung along with\u00a0 VFS Global Country Manager - Sri Lanka and Maldives Manpreet Singh Arora, at the inauguration ceremony\n\nStarting 21 August 2026, Korea visa applicants can visit our centrally located visa application centre in Colombo for a seamless application submission experience\n\nBooking a prior appointment is mandatory for applicants before visiting our centre for visa application submission\n\nVFS Global, the global leader in trusted technology services, empowering secure mobility for governments and citizens, has announced the launch of South Korea visa services in Sri Lanka through a state-of-the-art Korea Visa Application Centre in Colombo, providing an enhanced visa application experience for Korea visa applicants in the country.\n\nStarting 21 August 2026, Korea visa applicants across Sri Lanka will be able to submit their applications at the new Korea Visa Application Centre in Colombo by booking a prior appointment online.\n\nKorean Embassy in Sri Lanka Deputy Head of Mission Eunji Kang said, \u201cI hope that the Embassy\u2019s cooperation with VFS Global Visa Application Centre would contribute to providing greater convenience and improved services for visa applicants.\u201d\n\nVFS Global Chief Operating Officer - South Asia Yummi Talwar said, \u201cThe launch of our Korea Visa Application Centre marks a significant step in improving the visa application submission experience for travellers across Sri Lanka. This spacious, modern, and centrally located facility offers a comfortable and convenient application environment, supported by well-trained customer service representatives who will assist applicants at every step of their journey."
  },
