    "chunk_text": "VFS Global Chief Operating Officer - South Asia Yummi Talwar said, \u201cThe launch of our Korea Visa Application Centre marks a significant step in improving the visa application submission experience for travellers across Sri Lanka. This spacious, modern, and centrally located facility offers a comfortable and convenient application environment, supported by well-trained customer service representatives who will assist applicants at every step of their journey.\n\nVFS Global\u2019s role in the visa application process is limited to front-end administrative tasks only, which include collecting visa application forms, required documentation as per the checklist, and enroll biometrics. VFS Global has no role in the decision-making process of granting or refusing a visa. Decision making on the granting or refusal of visa is the sole prerogative and sole responsibility of the concerned Embassy.\n\nThe Korea Visa Application Centre in Colombo is located on the 2nd Floor of No. 657, Dr. Danister de Silva Mawatha, Colombo 09. Business hours are from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. Visa application submission hours are from 8:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m., while passport collection is available from 10:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.\n\nApplicants are encouraged to obtain the latest information on visa requirements, fees, appointment booking, and available services only through the official website of the Embassy of the Republic of Korea and the official VFS Global website.\n\nFor more information or to book an appointment, please visit https://visaforkorea-sl.com"
