    "chunk_text": "On Friday, Khan was taken back to jail just hours after being moved to Islamabad's private Shifa International Hospital for medical checks ordered by the Supreme Court. His lawyers had approached the court over concerns about his health.\n\nKhan served as Pakistan's Prime Minister from 2018 to 2022 before being removed through a no-confidence vote during a political crisis involving his government and Pakistan's military establishment.\n\nSince then, he has faced multiple legal cases on corruption and other charges. Khan and his party, Pakistan Tehreek-e-Insaf (PTI), have maintained that the cases against him are politically motivated.\n\nHis arrest in May 2023 triggered protests across Pakistan, some of which turned violent and led to hundreds of arrests."
