    "md5": "bc4621d07ee1a4943c279521472d4b94",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1029,
    "chunk_text": "Missing Badulla Hospital specialist doctor found dead in Mahiyanganaya\n\nColombo, Aug. 24 (Daily Mirror) - The body of a specialist doctor attached to the Badulla Teaching Hospital, who had been reported missing, was found today (24) on a rock in the Mapakadawewa area of Mahiyanganaya.\n\nThe doctor, an anesthesiologist, had reported for duty at the hospital yesterday morning (23) before disappearing later in the day.\n\nPolice investigations, including the examination of CCTV footage, revealed that the doctor\u2019s car had traveled towards Mahiyanganaya through Meegahakiula.\n\nThe vehicle was later found abandoned last night near the 17th-milepost along the Badulla\u2013Mahiyanganaya canal road in the Mapakadawewa area.\n\nFollowing this discovery, a joint search operation involving the Police, Crime Scene Investigation officers and the Sri Lanka Army was launched this morning. The operation led to the discovery of the doctor\u2019s body.\n\nPolice are conducting further investigations into the circumstances surrounding the death."
