    "chunk_text": "During questioning, Basik reportedly provided information about additional properties allegedly linked to him. Police said he disclosed that he owns two houses and two mobile phone shops in Boralesgamuwa.\n\nMeanwhile, investigators probing Basik's assets have also uncovered information about a tuition teacher who allegedly maintained close links with him and assisted in laundering drug money through investments in hotel projects.\n\nAccording to police, the teacher fled to Thailand several months ago, around the time Basik was initially detained. Authorities are now considering steps to secure an international warrant in connection with the investigation.\n\nPolice said the teacher's wife has also recently left the country. Although no arrest warrant is currently in force against her, investigators believe the family has left Sri Lanka because of the teacher's alleged business and financial links with Basik.\n\nMeanwhile, two other alleged organized crime figures arrested in Dubai, Bus Lalith, alias \u201cLalith Kannangara\u201d, and underworld figure Kavishka Madushan Abeywickrama, alias \u201cWanathe Chathu\u201d \u2014 are expected to be brought back to Sri Lanka this week.\n\nA team headed by Senior Superintendent of Police Kamal Ariyawansa, Director of the Central Crime Investigation Bureau, together with officers from the State Intelligence Service and the CID, have travelled to Dubai on the instructions of the Inspector General of Police to facilitate their return.\n\nBus Lalith was arrested in Dubai in November 2025 at an apartment complex following information obtained after one of his close associates was arrested and questioned in Sri Lanka.\n\nWanathe Chathu, who is alleged to have been involved in drug distribution and organized criminal activities, was arrested in Ras Al Khaimah, Dubai. He had reportedly operated in the Borella and Wanathamulla areas and maintained connections with drug traffickers including Kalu Thushara and Anju."
