    "chunk_text": "SLPP to strengthen grassroots campaign ahead of elections: Namal\n\nColombo, Aug. 24 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) National Organiser and Parliamentarian Namal Rajapaksa said the party would strengthen its grassroots engagement by visiting communities across the country as it prepares for future elections.\n\nSpeaking to journalists at the SLPP headquarters on Nelum Mawatha today, Namal said the party had contributed to bringing the President closer to the people and would continue to focus on engaging directly with communities.\n\n\u201cWe have to go from village to village for the presidency today. We have been able to take the President from the AC room in Colombo 7 to the main road and bring him closer to the people,\u201d he said.\n\nCommenting on the proposed 22nd Amendment to the Constitution, Rajapaksa expressed concern over statements made by Government representatives regarding matters that could come before the judiciary.\n\nHe said that public comments appearing to anticipate court decisions could raise concerns about judicial independence.\n\nNamal also said that recent discussions on judicial independence had highlighted the importance of allowing courts to carry out their duties without political influence.\n\nTurning to several recent controversies, he said the Government should give greater attention to issues directly affecting the public, including the timely provision of fertiliser, the purchase of paddy, fuel concessions for fishermen, support for graduates and assistance to industries facing difficulties.\n\nHe said the Government should focus on fulfilling the commitments outlined in its policy programme while ensuring that investigations into allegations of wrongdoing were conducted fairly and transparently.\n\nReferring to recent investigation reports, Namal questioned whether some investigations may have focused on selected individuals and called for a comprehensive review of the findings."
