    "chunk_text": "He said the Government should focus on fulfilling the commitments outlined in its policy programme while ensuring that investigations into allegations of wrongdoing were conducted fairly and transparently.\n\nReferring to recent investigation reports, Namal questioned whether some investigations may have focused on selected individuals and called for a comprehensive review of the findings.\n\nNamal also expressed concerns regarding the proposed 22nd Amendment, saying any constitutional changes should be considered carefully and should not undermine public confidence in democratic institutions or the rule of law.\n\nMeanwhile, commenting on the potential impact of El Ni\u00f1o conditions, Namal said successive governments had previously prepared contingency plans based on forecasts of adverse weather conditions.\n\nHe urged the Government to take timely preventive measures and ensure that relevant institutions were adequately prepared to respond to potential weather-related challenges."
