    "chunk_text": "Crossing transactions accounted for approximately LKR 15.83 billion, representing nearly 94% of total equity turnover. CTHR.N recorded multiple crossings totaling approximately LKR 11.58 billion at LKR 575.00 per share, while CARG.N recorded crossings worth LKR 4.20 billion at LKR 700.00 per share. JKH.N also recorded a crossing valued at approximately LKR 46.53 million involving 2.34 million shares at LKR 19.90.\n\nForeign investors remained significant net sellers, recording a net foreign outflow of LKR 909.90 million during the session.\n\nCTHR.N was the strongest positive contributor to the ASPI, adding 11.37 points to the index. HAYC.N, JKH.N, SIRA.N and GRAN.N also provided support.\n\nCOMB.N recorded the largest negative contribution, reducing the ASPI by 9.39 points. MELS.N, BREW.N, CTC.N and RICH.N also weighed on the index.\n\nOverall, the session reflected a cautious start to the week, with both benchmark indices ending lower and market breadth remaining weak. Although turnover surged to an unusually high level, activity was heavily concentrated in crossings, while the sizeable foreign outflow and broad-based selling pressure pointed to subdued underlying market sentiment."
