    "chunk_size_bytes": 883,
    "chunk_text": "CCTV helps swiftly arrest bag thief at Pettah bus stand\n\nColombo, Aug. 24 (Daily Mirror) - A suspect who allegedly stole a passenger\u2019s bag at the Pettah bus stand was swiftly arrested with the assistance of CCTV surveillance, Sri Lanka Air Force personnel said.\n\nThe theft occurred yesterday (23) and was detected through the CCTV monitoring system at the newly established operations room at the upgraded Pettah bus stand.\n\nAir Force personnel on duty immediately identified the suspect and handed him over to the Police.\n\nThe CCTV surveillance system, established under the \u2018Clean Sri Lanka\u2019 project, operates 24 hours a day to enhance public safety and security at the bus stand.\n\nThe operations room is also equipped to provide rapid assistance in emergencies, including situations where passengers suddenly fall ill, meet with accidents or require other urgent assistance."
