    "md5": "04852c1ae17b884b633a7e4da960175d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1306,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cTHRIVE demonstrates the impact that can be achieved when government, development partners and communities work together to expand opportunities for women and strengthen resilient livelihoods,\u201d said Women and Child Affairs Ministry Additional Secretary (Development) Nilmini Herath.\n\nUN Women Sri Lanka Head of Office Ramaaya Salgado added: \u201cBy strengthening livelihoods, supporting resilience to climate and economic shocks, and expanding opportunities for leadership and participation, the project contributes to broader efforts to advance gender equality and women\u2019s empowerment. The partnerships reflected in this Steering Committee are essential to ensuring that these gains are sustainable and reach women across all six project districts.\u201d\n\nParticipants attended a Townhall, bringing together local government representatives, civil society organisations and community members. PSC members also visited women-led enterprises and a Value Addition Centre. They engaged with women entrepreneurs and community members to hear first-hand insights of their experiences. Participants observed how women-led businesses are adapting to climate change and other shocks, while considering how THRIVE will support stronger livelihoods, resilience and economic opportunities across project communities."
