    "chunk_text": "Indian nationals nabbed at BIA with cigarettes worth Rs. 834,000\n\nColombo, Aug. 25 (Daily mirror) - Two Indian nationals were arrested by officers of the Airport Police Narcotics Bureau (PNB) in the early hours of today (25) for allegedly attempting to illegally bring a consignment of Chinese-manufactured cigarettes worth approximately Rs. 834,000 into Sri Lanka and remove them from Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA).\n\nThe suspects are a 33-year-old man employed in the construction sector in India and a 38-year-old woman working as a schoolteacher in India.\n\nPolice said the two had purchased the cigarettes in China before travelling to Singapore and subsequently arriving at the BIA at around 12.25 a.m. today on Singapore Airlines flight SQ-468.\n\nThey had allegedly concealed 278 cartons containing 55,600 cigarettes of various brands manufactured in China inside three suitcases.\n\nThe two suspects are scheduled to be produced before the Negombo Magistrate\u2019s Court today for further investigations."
