    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a23b4116f79996ad5d4a465271123992",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1834,
    "chunk_text": "VFS Global launches Republic of Korea visa services in Sri Lanka\n\nMiyon Lee, Former Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Sri Lanka and Maldives (second from left), Jung Haesung, Third Secretary and Consul, Embassy of the Republic of Korea (third from left) along with Manpreet Singh Arora, Country Manager, Sri Lanka and Maldives, VFS Global at the inauguration ceremony.\n\nVFS Global has announced the launch of South Korea visa services in Sri Lanka through a state-of-the-art Korea Visa Application Centre in Colombo, providing an enhanced visa application experience for Korea visa applicants in the country.\n\nStarting 21 August 2026, Korea visa applicants across Sri Lanka will be able to submit their applications at the new Korea Visa Application Centre in Colombo by booking a prior appointment online.\n\nEunji KANG, Deputy Head of Mission of the Embassy of the Republic of Korea in Sri Lanka, said, \u201cI hope that the Embassy\u2019s cooperation with VFS Global Visa Application Centre would contribute to providing greater convenience and improved services for visa applicants.\u201d\n\nYummi Talwar, Chief Operating Officer - South Asia, VFS Global, said, \u201cThe launch of our Korea Visa Application Centre marks a significant step in improving the visa application submission experience for travellers across Sri Lanka. This spacious, modern, and centrally located facility offers a comfortable and convenient application environment, supported by well-trained customer service representatives who will assist applicants at every step of their journey.\n\nVFS Global has been a trusted partner for the Government of the Republic of Korea for visa processing services since 2011. The company offers visa services on behalf of the Republic of Korea across 5 countries through a network of 7 dedicated visa application centres globally."
  },
