    "description": "ACL Cables\u2019 Fire Guard secures SLSI Certification",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/ACL-Cables-Fire-Guard-secures-SLSI-Certification/273-348811",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1787635938.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-25-dailymirrorlk-db122f00-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "98ba895a9a040c979c780b7c091fe50c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1806,
    "chunk_text": "ACL Cables\u2019 Fire Guard secures SLSI Certification\n\nSuren Madanayake, Managing Director, ACL Cables PLC receives the certification from Dr. Siddhika G. Senaratne, Director General and Chief Executive Officer, Sri Lanka Standards Institution (SLSI)\n\nCable manufacturer ACL Cables PLC has been officially granted a Sri Lanka Standards Institution (SLSI) permit to use the SLS Certification Mark for its FireGuard brand of flame-retardant electric cables.\n\nThe certification, issued under SLS 733 Part 2:2025 \u2013 Specification for Electric Cables for Voltages up to and including 300/500V, PVC Insulated and PVC Sheathed Flame Retardant (FR) Cables, validates ACL\u2019s commitment to uncompromising safety and quality. ACL is the first cable manufacturer in Sri Lanka to be certified under this standard.\n\nThe milestone directly strengthens ACL\u2019s Purple Standard \u2013 the industry benchmark introduced by ACL through its FireGuard range, distinguished through its purple sheath identity. The Purple Standard has become synonymous with flame\u2011retardant performance, consumer trust, and regulatory compliance in Sri Lanka. Securing the SLS certification mark, ACL demonstrates the Purple Standard has evolved from a pioneering manufacturer innovation into a nationally validated benchmark for protection.\n\nFor over 20 years, ACL FireGuard has maintained a benchmark for advanced fire safety in flame-retardant cables. As Sri Lanka now formalises a national standard for the category, ACL is moving beyond that benchmark, continuing to advance safety, performance, and expectations across the industry.\n\nAs the pioneers of flame-retardant cables in Sri Lanka, ACL had already been manufacturing FireGuard to this same standard of performance for more than 20 years before the SLS certification made it official."
  },
