    "language": "en",
    "md5": "183cddc136b9eb1ab3db0042c8911e9c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1851,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cI am also looking forward to exploring the possibility of raising new capital with my long-term business partner for over 25 years, Dato Sri Vijay Eswaran. Our partner Vijay has been a passionate and bullish investor in Sri Lanka because of his roots to Sri Lanka just like myself, and he entered this during some of the country\u2019s most challenging years. His connection to Sri Lanka and his origins in the country have shaped a deep conviction in its long-term potential.\u201d Raju Radha stressed.\n\n\u201cWhat characterizes him best is that he has remained faithful to his convictions and persevered with what he started. He recognized the true long-term potential of Sri Lanka much before the war ended. That conviction, built through decades of experience and belief in the country\u2019s future, is particularly relevant today as Sri Lanka enters a new phase of economic transformation\u201d Radha further said.\n\nThe potential capital-raising initiative could provide GLPL with additional financial firepower to pursue new development opportunities, enhance its existing asset base and capitalize on the evolving commercial real estate landscape in Colombo. The potential partnership would bring together Radha\u2019s deep domestic real estate footprint and Eswaran\u2019s international commercial capacity and long-standing confidence in Sri Lanka, bringing fresh strategic direction to GLPL as Sri Lanka\u2019s property sector experiences renewed momentum.\n\nTransitioning Green Lanka Towers into a fully self-sustained asset provides the company with substantial operational agility. The management is pivoting its focus toward facility modernization, asset optimization, and tailored commercial real estate solutions designed for institutional occupiers, while assessing opportunities to expand its footprint through new investments and strategic acquisitions."
  },
