    "chunk_size_bytes": 1227,
    "chunk_text": "The company\u2019s payments to the state climbed 20.4 percent to Rs.116.57 billion during the year ended March 31, 2026, from Rs.96.86 billion a year earlier.\n\nThe total was equivalent to about 71 percent of DCSL\u2019s standalone gross turnover of Rs.164.38 billion. The excise duties alone rose 20.7 percent to Rs.102.90 billion, from Rs.85.26 billion.\n\nAt group level, profit after tax rose 16.3 percent to Rs.17.07 billion, supported by the contribution and continued integration of DCSL Breweries Lanka Ltd.\n\nDCSL said the improved macroeconomic conditions, including lower inflation and a more stable rupee, had yet to translate fully into stronger household purchasing power. Consumer spending remained cautious, due to the high cost of living and repeated tax adjustments, particularly affecting the discretionary and price-sensitive products such as alcohol.\n\nThe company called for a balanced fiscal and regulatory framework that protects the government revenue while allowing the legitimate producers to compete with the illicit market.\n\nFor 2026/27, DCSL plans to focus on brewery integration, automation at its Seeduwa facility and supply-chain improvements to contain the costs as the tax and excise pressures continue."
