    "chunk_text": "Having built end-to-end operational capabilities across its domestic fleet, the company is evaluating plans to offer these repair and maintenance services to the third-party operators locally, before expanding into the wider South Asian corridor \u2014 alongside its civil engineering and plant lifecycle management expertise, leveraging its existing overseas footprint to capture the cross-border opportunities.\n\nThe IPP is looking to build hard-currency, US dollar-denominated revenue through further geographic expansion, reducing its reliance on a single off-taker and mitigating the domestic foreign exchange exposure.\n\nDomestically, the group is also formulating repowering programmes across its pioneer utility-scale wind farms, under which the ageing turbines in the proven high-density wind corridors will be replaced with the next-generation, higher-capacity models to lift the energy output per site footprint.\n\nWindForce Managing Director Manjula Perera said long-term value creation requires continuous technological diversification alongside operational agility.\n\n\u201cAs a renewable energy company, our mission extends beyond generating electricity; we are committed to creating lasting value for our stakeholders while contributing to a cleaner, more resilient and energy-secure future for Sri Lanka,\u201d Perera said, adding that the group\u2019s development pipeline spanning solar, wind, floating solar and battery storage positions it to capture the emerging opportunities.\n\nThe focus on engineering commercialisation and repowering comes as the private renewable developers navigate the finite lifecycles governing Sri Lanka\u2019s power purchase agreements.\n\nWindForce\u2019s generation portfolio operates under 20-year standard PPAs signed with the NSO and with the early installations advancing through their contract tenures, the group has identified fixed-term PPAs as a transition risk requiring proactive lifecycle planning to prevent asset stranding and manage long-term decommissioning liabilities."
  },
