    "chunk_text": "The fixed broadband subscriptions stood at 2.02 million. Across all 2.71 million fixed-line connections \u2014 spanning both voice and data services \u2014 LTE technology dominated, with a 60 percent share, followed by fibre at 19 percent, while the legacy copper and ADSL lines held 14 percent and 6 percent, respectively.\n\nInternational outgoing voice traffic fell to 11.28 million minutes in the first half of 2026. That migration is underlined by the mobile social media engagement, where WhatsApp and Facebook led the market with 16.54 million and 16.50 million users, respectively, closely followed by YouTube, with 16.00 million users and TikTok, with 13.61 million users as of mid-2026.\n\nThe sector\u2019s workforce continued to consolidate even as network automation and digital self-care adoption expanded. Total direct employment across the mobile and fixed access operators held broadly steady at 9,074 in June 2026, up slightly from 9,066 a year earlier but still well below the 12,498 jobs the industry reported 15 years ago."
