    "chunk_text": "The scheme allows the eligible borrowers to obtain up to Rs.75 million at concessionary rates for paddy purchases. A further Rs.7.5 billion was allocated for the 2026 Yala season to support the purchases at the government-guaranteed price, with loans of up to Rs.25 million offered interest-free.\n\nFifteen state and private banks are participating in the financing programme, which is administered by the Finance Ministry\u2019s Development Finance Department.\n\nMore than 70 percent of lending has reportedly been directed outside the Western province, reversing the concentration of previous credit programmes in Colombo and Gampaha. The ministry, however, did not provide a district-level breakdown of disbursements.\n\nWhile the rapid utilisation indicates a strong demand for subsidised credit, the available data do not show the repayment performance, employment generated or the additional economic output created through the programme."
