    "chunk_text": "He warned that arbitrary outgrower and revenue-sharing models could become \u201cdisguised informalisation\u201d if workers lost guaranteed earnings, EPF, ETF, leave, maternity protection, collective bargaining and termination safeguards.\n\n\u201cProductivity reform is necessary, but efficiency cannot mean transferring every commercial risk from the company to the worker,\u201d he said.\n\nHe added that digital labour and export systems also required proper cybersecurity and data protection, noting that the Online Safety Act was not a substitute for a comprehensive Cyber Security Act.\n\n\u201cThis is not merely a Tamil, plantation or trade-union issue. The person plucking tea, stitching garments, processing rubber, building boats or coding export services is earning Sri Lanka\u2019s foreign exchange. Economic patriotism begins by protecting the hand that earns the dollar,\u201d Arullsamy said."
