    "md5": "e7e3200f2b2f2a1674a910ad30fde715",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "Police reveal charges against \u2018Bus Lalith\u2019 after Dubai repatriation\n\nColombo, Aug. 25 (Daily Mirror) - Police today revealed the charges against Lalith Kannangara, alias \u201cBus Lalith,\u201d following his repatriation from Dubai, where he had been hiding under Interpol Red Notice, with the suspect wanted in connection with multiple cases of murder, attempted murder, drug trafficking, extortion, arson and serious assault.\n\nA team of officers led by the Director of the Central Crime Investigation Bureau (CCIB) escorted the 36-year-old suspect, who arrived in Sri Lanka in the early hours of August 25.\n\nKannangara, a resident of Kalutara South, is wanted in connection with a series of serious offences reported across several police divisions, including murder, attempted murder, assault, extortion, arson and firearms-related offences.\n\nAccording to police records, he is accused of assaulting and injuring a person with a sharp weapon in the Hanwella Police area in September 2013.\n\nHe is also wanted in connection with an incident in 2021 in which a business premises in Neluwathuduwa was allegedly broken into and a lorry was set on fire. In another incident that year, he allegedly opened fire near a businessman\u2019s residence after extortion demands were refused, seriously injuring the victim.\n\nPolice said Kannangara is further wanted over an October 2022 incident in which three people were allegedly attacked and seriously injured after a group forcibly entered a house in the Hanwella Police area.\n\nHe is also accused of aiding, abetting and conspiring in the fatal shooting of a person on Cross Street, Hanwella, on December 18, 2022. The case is currently before the Homagama/Awissawella Magistrate\u2019s Court.\n\nPolice records also link him to the double shooting murder of two people in the Padukka Police area on December 25, 2023, and the fatal shooting of another person in the Hanwella area on March 4, 2024."
  },
