    "chunk_size_bytes": 1896,
    "chunk_text": "Police records also link him to the double shooting murder of two people in the Padukka Police area on December 25, 2023, and the fatal shooting of another person in the Hanwella area on March 4, 2024.\n\nIn 2025, Kannangara allegedly opened fire at three people travelling in a three-wheeler in the Kosgama Police area, injuring them. Police also accuse him of supplying a T-56 assault rifle and 25 rounds of ammunition to a person arrested near a nightclub in Kollupitiya in July 2025.\n\nHe is further accused of directing the fatal shooting of a former Pradeshiya Sabha member who was travelling on a motorcycle in the Meegoda Police area on August 12, 2025. The following day, a firearm was allegedly discharged into the air on Muthuhena Road in the Meegoda area before the suspects fled.\n\nPolice Media Spokesperson and Assistant Superintendent of Police F.U. Wootler said the arrest followed special intelligence received by the Inspector General of Police on October 25, 2025.\n\nThe suspect is currently in the custody of the Central Crime Investigation Bureau for further investigations. Police said inquiries will also focus on his alleged involvement in drug trafficking, other organised criminal activities and properties suspected to have been acquired through illegal means.\n\nThe Illegal Assets Investigation Unit has launched a separate investigation into the suspect\u2019s assets.\n\nASP Wootler said that since 2024, police have repatriated 42 suspects against whom Interpol Red Notices had been issued. Steps are also being taken to bring back a further 109 individuals wanted under Red Notices.\n\nIn addition, 38 suspects who did not have Red Notices have been repatriated, with several more expected to be brought back in the coming days.\n\nPolice also said action has been taken over the past three years to confiscate illicitly acquired assets valued at approximately Rs. 3.878 billion."
