    "chunk_text": "Meanwhile, Conservator of Forests (Protection and Law Enforcement) Wasantha Gajanayake said the number of forest crimes reported during the first eight months of this year has decreased compared to the corresponding period last year.\n\nHe attributed the decline mainly to the Forest Protection Unit established in 1995 and said members of the public have continued to provide information about forest crimes.\n\nGajanayake also warned of an increase in forest fires amid dry conditions linked to the prevailing El Ni\u00f1o-related weather pattern.\n\nHe said some fires had spread into forests after being deliberately set to clear farmland, while others had allegedly been started for hunting or for entertainment.\n\nStrict legal action is being taken against those responsible for setting forest fires and committing other forest offences under the Forest Conservation Ordinance, he said.\n\nThe Ministry of Environment has also launched several programmes aimed at strengthening environmental protection and conserving Sri Lanka\u2019s ecosystems for future generations."
