    "chunk_text": "For de Zoysa, leadership is not about creating employees who remain dependent on the person at the top. It is about developing people capable of thinking and acting independently, while ensuring that credit goes to those responsible for an achievement.\n\nThat principle perhaps best captures a career that did not follow the conventional route.\n\nHis story also offers a broader lesson for a generation entering a business environment increasingly focused on qualifications and credentials: formal education can open doors, but it is not the only measure of future potential.\n\nExperience, resilience, integrity and the ability to work with people can prove equally decisive."
