    "language": "en",
    "md5": "abd3e57cc93a19aee365f71e64244b5c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1806,
    "chunk_text": "Vista Essential Foods enters local spice market, unveils export ambitions\n\nFrom left: Vista Essential Foods Managing Director Suhanya\u00a0 Perera\u00a0 Ockersz, Chairman Quintus Perera\u00a0 and General Manager Nilmin Arsacularatne at the launching of its spice range at Hilton Colombo.\n\nWith worldwide demand increasing for authentic and high-quality spices, a new entrant to Sri Lanka\u2019s food manufacturing and distribution scene has disclosed major plans for export market entry.\n\nLaunching seven of its flagship spice products to the local market in Colombo last week, Vista Essential Foods (Pvt) Ltd said it looks forward to gradually scale-up and enter export markets in the future, while establishing its presence locally.\n\n\u201cWe have already received inquiries from Singapore, Malaysia, Azerbaijan, and Germany. It\u2019s a very encouraging development at this stage. Compliance with international standards is key to enter these export markets, and there are certain globally recognised food safety and quality standards certifications such as the Brand Reputation through Compliance Global Standards (BRCGS), HACCP, FSSC 22000 (Food Safety System Certification 22000) etc essential to enter and get a solid footing particularly in European markets,\u201d Vista Essential Foods Managing Director Suhanya\u00a0 Perera\u00a0 Ockersz\u00a0 told Mirror Business.\n\nBRCGS are global food safety standards that are heavily preferred or required by major European supermarkets and food processors, while HACCP is a mandatory food safety procedure required by EU law for all external food businesses. FSSC 22000 on the other hand is a core food safety management system standard widely accepted by major global markets because it has official recognition from the Global Food Safety Initiative (GFSI), the Managing Director explained."
  },
