    "chunk_size_bytes": 1311,
    "chunk_text": "BRCGS are global food safety standards that are heavily preferred or required by major European supermarkets and food processors, while HACCP is a mandatory food safety procedure required by EU law for all external food businesses. FSSC 22000 on the other hand is a core food safety management system standard widely accepted by major global markets because it has official recognition from the Global Food Safety Initiative (GFSI), the Managing Director explained.\n\nSri Lanka currently produces a wide variety of high-quality spices. According to the Export Development Board, the country exports around 30,000 tons of various kinds of spices annually, and over 90 percent of spice and allied products manufactured in Sri Lanka are consumed by the global food and beverage industry, the pharmaceutical industry, and the personal care products industry. In terms of market outlook, the local spices sector is projected to witness mixed growth rate patterns during 2025 to 2029. Accordingly, the growth rate begins at 8.89 percent in 2025, climbs to a high of 9.83 percent in 2026, and moderates to 9.81 percent by 2029.\n\nVista Essential Foods\u2019 initial range of spice products includes Chilli Powder, Chilli Pieces, Curry Powder, Roasted Curry Powder, Roasted Chilli Powder, Turmeric Powder, and Pepper Powder."
