    "md5": "f0f48e9aa15cfcb862829cba3a6079f4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1881,
    "chunk_text": "Universal Gateway Holdings accelerates F&B growth with twin Colombo launch\n\nUniversal Gateway Holdings (Pvt) Ltd has bolstered its footprint in Sri Lanka\u2019s hospitality sector with the launch of a novel dual-dining concept, Thai Fusion and Global Kitchen, operating under one roof at 60, Davidson Road, Colombo 4, adjacent to Duplication Road.\n\nSpeaking to Mirror Business following the launch , Universal Gateway Holdings Chairman and Managing Director Mohamed Afthab outlined an ambitious regional growth strategy that aims to expand the group\u2019s restaurant portfolio from its current 11 branches to between 30 and 40 outlets across Sri Lanka and the region over the next three to four years.\n\n\u201cThe food and beverage sector under Universal Gateway Holdings is growing rapidly,\u201d Afthab said. \u201cOur vision is not simply to increase the number of restaurants, but to introduce distinctive concepts and cuisines to the Sri Lankan market while maintaining high standards across our brands\u201d.\n\nThe newly unveiled five-storey establishment in Bambalapitiya operates daily from 11:00 a.m. to 11:00 p.m., catering to corporate diners, families, and international visitors. \u201cOur objective is to develop strong restaurant concepts that offer premium quality food, consistency and memorable dining experiences,\u201d he added.\n\nOccupying the ground and mezzanine levels, Thai Fusion delivers an authentic fine-dining experience led by a specialized team of gourmet chefs brought in from Thailand. With a seating capacity of 70, the venue offers an artfully crafted menu featuring traditional Thai salads, soups, fragrant curries, fresh seafood specialties, and signature desserts.\n\n\u201cWith Thai Fusion, we are particularly focused on maintaining authenticity, and following its establishment, we intend to expand the brand to other key locations around Sri Lanka,\u201d Afthab explained."
  },
