    "chunk_size_bytes": 1210,
    "chunk_text": "Packeted tea accounted for much of the decline, with shipments falling by 4.69 million kilograms to 63.89 million kilograms. Bulk tea exports dropped by 2.73 million kilograms to 59.92 million kilograms.\n\nThe cumulative average FOB value rose to Rs. 1,826.16 per kilogram during January-July from Rs. 1,748.51 a year earlier. In dollar terms, however, the average fell to US$5.70 from US$5.86.\n\nAll export categories except instant tea recorded higher FOB values in rupee terms during the seven-month period. In dollar terms, green tea was the only segment to post an increase.\n\nT\u00fcrkiye remained Sri Lanka\u2019s largest tea export destination, with shipments reaching 24.76 million kilograms, up 138 percent year-on-year from 10.40 million kilograms.\n\nIraq retained second place despite imports falling 36 percent to 14.42 million kilograms, while Russia ranked third with 13.35 million kilograms, up 2.6 percent. Azerbaijan recorded a 49 percent increase to 7.14 million kilograms, placing it fourth. China followed with 5.59 million kilograms, down 8 percent, while exports to Libya plunged 58 percent to 5.41 million kilograms.\n\nJordan, Chile, Saudi Arabia and Syria completed the top 10 export destinations."
