    "language": "en",
    "md5": "7fbc6c35c29ef20dbfb425a941f4d30d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 945,
    "chunk_text": "People want stability. They want to know that their savings are safe, that their jobs will remain secure, that prices will not suddenly explode and that the country will not once again return to the desperate conditions experienced during the last crisis.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery is too important to become a contest in political point scoring. The country cannot afford another crisis created by economic mismanagement. The lesson from 2022 should be clear to everyone.\n\nEconomic stability is not something politicians should gamble with. Sri Lanka needs less political theatre and more economic truth. It needs politicians who will compete over solutions rather than predictions of disaster. And above all, it needs leaders who understand that when they speak about the economy, they are not merely addressing a political audience.\n\nThey are speaking to an entire nation still recovering from its worst economic trauma in generations."
  },
