    "chunk_text": "The country had previously been placed in the restricted-default category following the suspension of external debt repayments during the crisis. It has since moved out of that category and into speculative-grade territory following progress in restructuring its debt.\n\n\u201cWe are hopeful that Sri Lanka will soon receive a further upgrade, reflecting the progress that has been achieved,\u201d he said.\n\nA further sovereign rating upgrade would provide an external assessment of the improvement in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic and fiscal position, although the country remains below investment grade.\n\nImproved sovereign creditworthiness could also help rebuild international investor confidence as Sri Lanka gradually seeks to normalise its relationship with global capital markets following the default.\n\nThe recovery, however, will increasingly be judged on whether the macroeconomic stability achieved since the crisis can translate into sustained growth, investment and greater resilience against future domestic and external shocks.\n\nWeerasinghe reiterated that Sri Lanka\u2019s experience could offer lessons beyond the country itself, particularly for international financial institutions and businesses assessing how economies can emerge from severe balance-of-payments crises.\n\nHe said Sri Lanka could increasingly be viewed as an example of how a country can recover quickly from a deep economic crisis while laying the foundations for a more stable, resilient and sustainable economy."
