    "md5": "a3b285572d8dd10e20b12b507d427e84",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1098,
    "chunk_text": "The prosecution case was supported by several eyewitnesses, including passengers and other road users. The Court observed that witnesses testified to the bus travelling at a terrifying speed and swaying dangerously before the collision.\n\nThe accused had claimed that the three-wheeler driver had attempted a sudden U-turn, resulting in the accident. He also admitted that he had been travelling at excessive speed.\n\nThe accused was charged with seven counts under Section 298 of the Penal Code for causing death by a rash or negligent act, 21 counts under Section 329 for causing grievous hurt by an act endangering human life, and 24 counts under Section 328 for causing hurt in similar circumstances.\n\nFollowing a lengthy trial, the High Court sentenced him to one year of rigorous imprisonment on each of the seven Section 298 counts, three months on each of the Section 329 counts and one month on each of the Section 328 counts. The sentences were ordered to run consecutively, resulting in a total of 13 years and three months' rigorous imprisonment, together with fines totalling Rs. 55,800."
