    "md5": "333a91d63afc49f21eb2c6b159085643",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1591,
    "chunk_text": "Fire kills 14 newborns at major hospital in Pakistan, officials say\n\neuro news. - A fire at a hospital's maternity ward in a major government hospital in Pakistan\u2019s capital killed at least 14 newborn babies early on Wednesday, according to hospital officials and the government.\n\nThe fire broke out on the third floor of the Mother and Child Health Ward at the public Pakistan Institute of Medical Sciences (PIMS) hospital, according to the district administration.\n\nRescue officials said the fire broke out at around 6:45 am (3:45 am CEST) after an air-conditioning unit compressor apparently exploded inside the nursery, located in the hospital\u2019s gynecology ward.\n\nSohail Ashraf, the Islamabad chief commissioner, said on X that rescue teams, specialists, police and himself \"immediately reached at site and controlled the fire.\"\n\nPrime Minister Shehbaz Sharif expressed sorrow over the deaths and ordered an immediate investigation.\n\n\u201cThe loss of children in such circumstances is irreparable,\u201d a statement from his office said.\n\nSharif also expressed his \u201cheartfelt condolences to the families of the innocent children,\u201d adding that he was \u201csaddened by this tragic incident.\u201d.\n\nPolice said the newborns killed in the fire were severely burned, making DNA testing necessary to confirm their identities before their bodies can be released to their families.\n\nThe statement came after parents called for the bodies to be handed over immediately.\n\nFires in large buildings are frequent in Pakistan, often due to poor safety laws and building codes as well as lax enforcement."
  },
