    "chunk_text": "Union urges railways to withdraw legal action against SLRSMU Chief Secretary\n\nColombo, Aug. 26 (Daily Mirror) - The Joint Development Officers\u2019 Union has urged the General Manager of Sri Lanka Railways to immediately withdraw the decision to initiate legal action against the Chief Secretary of the Sri Lanka Railways Station Masters\u2019 Union (SLRSMU) for publicly highlighting shortcomings in the administration of the Railway Department.\n\nMeanwhile, the SLRSMU has called for an urgent investigation into the recent breakdowns of locomotive engines, alleging that the current Railway General Manager should also be among those scrutinised over the incidents.\n\nSLRSMU General Secretary Kasun Chamara, speaking to the media, said a proper investigation would establish responsibility for the repeated locomotive failures. He alleged that the Railway General Manager was responsible for the current situation.\n\nAddressing the media, the Joint Development Officers\u2019 Union Secretary said a letter had reportedly been issued seeking legal action against the SLRSMU Chief Secretary nearly one year after the General Manager assumed office.\n\nHe stressed that trade unions have the right to express their views on matters concerning their services and issues faced by their members.\n\n\u201cThis is something the General Manager, Ministers, Secretaries, Deputy Ministers and all senior management officials should understand,\u201d he said.\n\nThe union secretary said the General Manager had held several discussions with trade unions regarding their grievances, but claimed that the issues raised by the unions had not been properly resolved.\n\nHe alleged that the move to initiate legal action against a trade union official could be seen as an attempt to suppress trade union activities.\n\n\u201cAlthough these issues have been discussed at various levels, the real problems have not been resolved,\u201d he said."
