    "md5": "8aae2e442f79e4c78394ed7cdbe8e3d3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1814,
    "chunk_text": "133 Indians missing in Nepal flash flood; 95 killed; Bihar, UP borders on alert\n\nINDIA TODAY - At least 133 Indians are among the over 400 persons missing with at least 95 deaths confirmed after massive flash floods swept through Nepal\u2019s northern Rasuwa district near the Tibet border on Wednesday, washing away homes, vehicles, bridges and infrastructure project sites. The disaster has also triggered an alert in Bihar, which shares a border with Nepal, as floodwaters continue to move downstream.\n\nThe surge entered the river Bhote Koshi from the Tibetan side around 9 am, severely affecting Timure and Syapru Besi, officials said. A mudslide also struck Tibet near the Gyirong border crossing, causing casualties and leaving people missing, China's state-run Xinhua reported.\n\nSecurity footage from the Chinese side of the Nepal-Tibet border captured people fleeing moments before a massive torrent of rocks, mud and water tore through the area, destroying buildings and vehicles and claiming several lives. The exact cause of the mudslide remained uncertain.\n\nHowever, the German Research Centre for Geosciences (GFZ) reported that a 4.4-magnitude earthquake struck around seven minutes before the timestamp visible on the security footage.\n\nVideos circulating on social media showed rivers raging through the region, with one showing floodwaters sweeping away a bridge. Another video showed a house collapsing like a pack of cards as people screamed and ran in panic in the background.\n\nThe Nepal government initiated rescue operations in flood-hit areas, but helicopters were unable to land in places where the floodwater levels are high. Chinese President Xi Jinping called for an all-out search for those missing in Tibet and stronger monitoring and early-warning systems to prevent secondary disasters."
