    "md5": "05142ecbd7165bffa3d03d8fe159e251",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1041,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan embassy issues urgent safety advisory due to Nepal floods\n\nColombo, August 27 (Daily Mirror) - The Sri Lankan Embassy in Kathmandu has issued an urgent safety advisory to Sri Lankan nationals in Nepal following a sudden flash flood that entered Rasuwa district through the Bhote Koshi River from the Tibetan side.\n\nThe flood has caused significant damage in the Timure and Syabrubesi areas and raised concerns along downstream sections of the Bhote Koshi and Trishuli rivers.\n\nSri Lankans in Rasuwa, Nuwakot, Dhading, Gorkha, Chitwan and other areas along the river corridors have been urged to avoid rivers, riverbanks, bridges and low-lying areas and to follow instructions from local authorities and security agencies.\n\nThose planning to travel to affected areas have been advised to postpone their journeys until the flood threat subsides and road conditions are confirmed safe.\n\nSri Lankan nationals needing urgent assistance can contact the Embassy's 24-hour emergency hotline on +977 9851048653 or email [email\u00a0protected]."
