    "md5": "715b1c6b43ad4a66a7b3110b15320a9f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1676,
    "chunk_text": "We still remain dependent on remittances of expatriate workers to meet costs of imports as well as to repay our external debt by 2028. Government\u2019s failure to fulfill many of its post-election promises has taken toll of its popularity among the masses. Today we are beginning to hear even drivers of three-wheeled vehicles (among the government\u2019s main propagandists earlier) now berating the President and his men in the language of Billingsgate.\n\nThe Minister assured us citizens his government had not paid themselves any salary increase. It was,\u00a0 the Minister said, merely an entitlement of a specified quantity of fuel, with the corresponding allowance calculated based on revised fuel prices.\n\nUnfortunately,\u00a0 this entitlement has not been made available to the rest of us ordinary citizens.\n\nWith problems faced by the people increasing, the government\u2019s popularity today is at a new low. The ruling party too,\u00a0 has seen \u2018the writing on the wall\u2019. The refusal to hold the constitutionally required Provincial Council election in a timely fashion is a clear indication government is afraid to expose the drop in its popularity.\n\nWhat is most awkward however is the present government appears to be trying to deceive big brother across the Palk Straits that they intend to speedily hold Provincial Council Elections.\u00a0 The reality is that the present government has taken no practical steps to implement that promise.\n\nWhile the country is facing this plethora of mega problems, our politicians of the political opposition and the government, like the Roman Emperor \u2018Nero\u2019 of old, are fiddling while our country is sinking further and further into a mess."
  },
