    "md5": "9a3e2cada683edd27c85dac1b7fa7956",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 863,
    "chunk_text": "According to his petition, the Twenty-Second Amendment Bill seeks to increase the retirement age of judges of the Supreme Court and Court of Appeal, make provision regarding the retirement date of the Chief Justice and increase the number of judges of the Court of Appeal.\n\nHe further argues that the proposed amendment falls within the legislative competence of Parliament and does not require approval by the people at a referendum under Article 83.\n\nThe NPP MP has also requested the Court to declare or order that the Twenty-Second Amendment Bill as a whole and/or any of its clauses is not inconsistent with Article 3 of the Constitution and does not require approval at a referendum.\n\nHe has further sought the dismissal of the BASL petition, refusal of the reliefs sought by the BASL petitioners, costs and any other relief the Court considers appropriate."
