    "chunk_size_bytes": 1307,
    "chunk_text": "It said judicial judgments, judicial conduct and the administration of justice could properly be subjected to fair, informed and responsible criticism. Where credible concerns or allegations arise concerning any member of the Judiciary, including the Chief Justice, such matters should be examined objectively and addressed through the appropriate Constitutional and parliamentary processes, with due regard to fairness and due process.\n\nAt the same time, the BASL urged all parties to act responsibly when making allegations against individual judges, lawyers and others.\n\nThe BASL further emphasised that judicial independence should not be regarded as a shield against legitimate scrutiny or accountability. Rather, it said judicial independence is a safeguard for the people, ensuring that disputes are determined impartially and that individual rights, the Rule of Law and the Constitutional order are protected.\n\nThe BASL called on all organs of the State, relevant parties and the media to respect the role of the Judiciary and the system of administration of justice, while ensuring that genuine concerns are addressed fairly, responsibly and through procedures established by the Constitution and the law.\n\nThe statement was signed by BASL President Rajeev Amarasuriya and Secretary Nalin De Silva."
