    "chunk_text": "He further said that in 2016 a change was introduced where families of the disappeared were able to opt for a Certificate of Absence (CoA). \u201cMany families were quite nervous about accepting a certificate of disappeared. They thought the minute they accept a certificate of disappeared the government would close the file and that they wouldn\u2019t trace the individual. The CoA is therefore an attempt to try and provide some of the services you could access similarly to when you receive a certificate of death. But it is not expansive as a certificate of death. Based on OMP recommendations, 335 families have now obtained a certificate of absence,\u201d he added.\n\nWhen asked about the cases of missing inmates, OMP Chairman Mahesh Katulanda told the Daily Mirror that the OMP is following these cases. \u201cWe have received a formal complaint and we are now in the process of calling their close relatives to obtain statements as part of the investigations,\u201d he added."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-08-28-dailymirrorlk-a28011e8",
