    "md5": "a36f461d5fcd94fadd05625e1c69b043",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1963,
    "chunk_text": "Iran war: Intensified diplomacy raises hope for peace\n\nPakistan\u2019s military chief Asim Munir holds talks with Iran\u2019s President Masoud Pezeshkian in Tehran on Monday\n\nSpeculation is rife about a deal between the United States and Iran after a C\u201117 US military aircraft carrying CIA Director John Ratcliffe landed in Moscow on Tuesday. There are numerous issues to be thrashed out between the two big powers that were superpower rivals during the five\u2011decade Cold War.\n\nSome believe the talks concern the Ukraine war, which President Donald Trump had boasted he would end within his first week in office but failed to do. The war is not going well for Russia, with European powers enhancing their military and political support for Ukraine even as the US scales down its backing. The visit came amid an escalation in the Russia\u2011Ukraine conflict, with Ukraine demonstrating its newly gained military strength by striking strategic targets deep inside Russia. Meanwhile, Russia accused the Baltic states\u2014Latvia, Estonia, and Lithuania\u2014of allowing Ukraine to use their airspace to hit Russian targets, warning them and other NATO members, particularly Britain, that they would face consequences.\n\nAnalysts also believe Iran was high on the agenda during Ratcliffe\u2019s four\u2011hour unscheduled visit for talks with his counterpart. On Wednesday, in a one\u2011minute exclusive interview with Al Jazeera, Trump declined to comment on the CIA director\u2019s trip, citing the sensitivities involved. However, POLITICO reported that in a separate US radio interview, Trump denied speculation that Ratcliffe had travelled to Moscow to dissuade Putin from testing NATO\u2019s resolve or attacking Britain, which this week vowed to double down on its support for Ukraine. Trump described the visit as \u201csemi-routine\u201d but acknowledged it was aimed at bringing the war to a close. \u201cI hate to disappoint people. We would like to see the war with Ukraine end,\u201d he said."
  },
