    "md5": "68361c0363fc95d819a5c5e03bc99e4f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1973,
    "chunk_text": "Analysts also believe Iran was high on the agenda during Ratcliffe\u2019s four\u2011hour unscheduled visit for talks with his counterpart. On Wednesday, in a one\u2011minute exclusive interview with Al Jazeera, Trump declined to comment on the CIA director\u2019s trip, citing the sensitivities involved. However, POLITICO reported that in a separate US radio interview, Trump denied speculation that Ratcliffe had travelled to Moscow to dissuade Putin from testing NATO\u2019s resolve or attacking Britain, which this week vowed to double down on its support for Ukraine. Trump described the visit as \u201csemi-routine\u201d but acknowledged it was aimed at bringing the war to a close. \u201cI hate to disappoint people. We would like to see the war with Ukraine end,\u201d he said.\n\nThe CIA chief\u2019s Russia visit came a day after US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent threatened to expand sanctions on countries refusing to cut economic ties with Iran\u2014a warning analysts said was aimed particularly at Russia and China. Beyond defence and political cooperation, Russia and Iran maintain strong economic links through the Caspian Sea\u2014a strictly no\u2011go zone for NATO.\n\nThe US \u201cD\u2011Day\u201d for Iran was on Monday. But there was no Iranian surrender. Instead, Tehran dismissed the US economic warfare, saying it had endured worse and was well accustomed to surviving under sanctions.\n\nAs the war launched by the US and Israel to destroy Iran\u2019s nuclear programme and bring about regime change enters its seventh month today, Ratcliffe\u2019s visit to Russia may not have been aimed at warning Moscow, as US media speculated. Russia is far from beholden to US dictates. If the trip was meant to warn Russia on its own soil, it was an ultimate insult.\n\nA spymaster par excellence, President Vladimir Putin is not unaware of US and NATO schemes to destabilise his country. Given Russia\u2019s strong defence ties with Iran, it is unlikely Moscow will heed any US warning\u2014whether about Ukraine or Iran."
  },
  {
