    "chunk_size_bytes": 1004,
    "chunk_text": "Pathirage throws 92.07m to win Zurich Diamond League\n\nAUG.28 (Mirror Sports) - Sri Lanka\u2019s Rumesh Tharanga Pathirage produced another stunning performance, throwing 92.07m to win the men\u2019s javelin at the Zurich Diamond League.\n\nPathirage saved his best for his sixth and final attempt, breaking the 92-metre barrier for the second time this season.\n\nGrenada\u2019s Anderson Peters finished second with 86.93m, while Poland\u2019s Dawid Wegner took third with 85.16m.\n\nPathirage\u2019s latest victory adds to a remarkable breakthrough season. He produced a personal-best and world-leading 92.62m in Rome in June before winning in Lausanne with an 88.14m effort.\n\nThe Zurich victory further cements the Sri Lankan\u2019s status as one of the world\u2019s leading javelin throwers, with Pathirage currently topping the Diamond League qualification standings.\n\nPathirage will now turn his attention to the Diamond League Final in Brussels on September 4-5, where he will look to cap a remarkable season on another high."
