    "md5": "21b854509febab046fde7142872459f7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1849,
    "chunk_text": "How Sri Lanka can turn resources into riches\n\nColombo, Aug. 28 (Daily Mirror) - Switzerland, a landlocked nation devoid of precious metals or crude oil, stands as one of the world's richest economies. It thrives on precision machinery, pharmaceuticals, and high-end consumer goods like chocolate and watches, supported by the world's most trusted banking system. In stark contrast, Sri Lanka an island blessed with fertile soil, a surrounding ocean, valuable gems, and a highly educated populace remains a developing nation still grappling with economic turmoil. The question is not why Sri Lanka struggles, but why Switzerland succeeds, and how Sri Lanka can follow suit.\n\nSwitzerland\u2019s success is a masterclass in value addition. With limited natural resources, it imports raw materials like gold, platinum, and cocoa, transforming them into high-value exports that command global prices. The Swiss model relies on a highly skilled workforce, institutional stability, and a sharp focus on niche, high end manufacturing and finance. It is an economy built on precision, trust, and education, where companies like Nestl\u00e9 or Rolex generate more revenue than entire resource-rich nations.\n\nSri Lanka possesses almost every advantage Switzerland lacks. It has a strategic maritime location, a rich agricultural base (tea, rubber, coconut and spices), and a treasure trove of gems like blue sapphire and padparadsha Sapphire and minerals. Yet, the country has faced crippling economic crises, including a sovereign default in 2022 that led to shortages of fuel, food, and medicine.\n\nWhile Sri Lanka exports high quality garments, tea, and rubber, it often exports them with low value addition. The country ships raw materials and semi-processed goods, missing the opportunity to build a manufacturing ecosystem that could command Swiss like premiums."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-08-28-dailymirrorlk-8cef0931",
