    "md5": "caffd8d74bc7e39c37c1315116c655d5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1009,
    "chunk_text": "Pharmacists to launch one-day strike\n\nColombo, Aug. 28 (Daily Mirror) - The Government Pharmacists\u2019 Association has decided to launch a one-day strike from 8 a.m. on August 31, citing unresolved issues over the \u201cadditional service allowance\u201d paid to pharmacists.\n\nAccording to Association President Ajith P. Thilakaratne, the Health Secretary had issued a circular dated August 29, 2026, changing the official designation of the overtime allowance paid to pharmacists to \u201cadditional service allowance.\u201d\n\nHowever, he said the circular was subsequently cancelled due to pressure exerted by the medical service, without any acceptable reason being given for the decision.\n\nThilakaratne said the authorities had so far failed to provide an acceptable solution to the issues raised by pharmacists.\n\nHe said the association was therefore demanding that the relevant circular be implemented, adding that the one-day strike had been planned to pressure the authorities to enforce it if they failed to do so."
