    "chunk_text": "Nearly 500 killed, over 1,400 still missing due to Nepal floods\n\nRTE - Devastating floods on the Nepal-China border region this week have killed at least 547 people, Nepal's police have said.\n\nChinese state media earlier confirmed five dead following Wednesday's disaster, taking the total killed to at least 552.\n\nMore than 1,400 people are missing of which at least 540 are foreign nationals, including two Irish citizens, who have been named by the Nepalese Tourism Department as 46-year-old Santosh Sahu and 18-year-old Spandan Sahu.\n\nThe Department of Foreign Affairs said in a statement that it \"continues to closely monitor the situation following serious flooding in Nepal and, together with partners, is working to account for two Irish citizens visiting the area.\"\n\nA huge torrent of rock, ice, mud and debris cascaded through Himalayan mountain river systems after the collapse, and also led to the formation of a lake where water continued to collect and rise.\n\nThe lake's reservoir had topped 2.5 million cubic metres of water, up from the estimated 1.5-2 million cubic metres recorded yesterday, before overflowing into the Bhotekoshi River, authorities in Nepal said.\n\nPeople ran to higher ground carrying belongings as announcements were made warning them to stay away from the river and police personnel remained on standby with ropes and stretchers.\n\nRescue workers were also asked to move to safer places along with their equipment.\n\nThe risk of the lake bursting prompted all Chinese rescue personnel and vehicles to withdraw and stand by in a safe area, state broadcaster CCTV said. Rescue operations \u200cwere later resumed \"as the risk posed by the upstream dammed lake was deemed manageable\", it \u2060said.\n\nAuthorities in Nepal stopped rescue operations for 90 minutes but resumed later, an army officer said.\n\nThe Nepali military was seeking to reach 100 people trapped in a tunnel of Trishuli 3A hydropower project, an army spokesman told AFP."
