    "chunk_size_bytes": 1889,
    "chunk_text": "Parliament to convene for four days from September 8\n\nColombo, Aug. 28 (Daily Mirror) - Parliament is scheduled to convene from September 8 to 11, following a decision taken by the Committee on Parliamentary Business.\n\nThe decision was made at a recent meeting of the Committee held on August 20 under the chairmanship of Speaker Jagath Wickramaratne.\n\nOn Tuesday, September 8, parliamentary business under Standing Order 22(1) to (6) will be taken up from 9.30 a.m. to 10.00 a.m., followed by Questions for Oral Answers from 10.00 a.m. to 11.00 a.m. and questions under Standing Order 27(2) from 11.00 a.m. to 11.30 a.m.\n\nFrom 11.30 a.m. to 5.00 p.m., the House will debate for approval two Orders published in Extraordinary Gazettes Nos. 2489/22 and 2493/19 under the Motor Traffic Act (Chapter 203).\n\nThe Opposition\u2019s Motion at the Adjournment Time will then be taken up from 5.00 p.m. to 5.30 p.m.\n\nOn Wednesday, September 9, parliamentary business under Standing Order 22(1) to (6) will be taken up from 9.30 a.m. to 10.00 a.m., followed by Questions to the Prime Minister from 10.00 a.m. to 10.30 a.m., Questions for Oral Answers from 10.30 a.m. to 11.00 a.m., and questions under Standing Order 27(2) from 11.00 a.m. to 11.30 a.m.\n\nThe Second Reading debate on the Chief of Defence Staff (Repeal) Bill is scheduled from 11.30 a.m. to 5.00 p.m., followed by Questions at the Adjournment Time from 5.00 p.m. to 5.30 p.m.\n\nOn Thursday, September 10, Questions for Oral Answers will be taken up from 10.00 a.m. to 11.00 a.m., after the usual parliamentary business from 9.30 a.m. to 10.00 a.m. Questions under Standing Order 27(2) will follow from 11.00 a.m. to 11.30 a.m.\n\nFrom 11.30 a.m. to 5.00 p.m., Parliament will debate for approval a Resolution under the Women\u2019s Empowerment Act.\n\nThe Government\u2019s Motion at the Adjournment Time will be debated from 5.00 p.m. to 5.30 p.m."
