    "chunk_text": "Each house comprises two bedrooms, a living room, kitchen and bathroom, with approximately Rs. 3.2 million spent on each unit.\n\nEach family has also been provided with essential furniture and kitchen equipment worth around Rs. 175,000.\n\nMeanwhile, under the Indian Housing Programme to construct 4,000 houses, the President presided over the presentation of freehold title deeds to 163 beneficiaries residing in houses constructed in the Haldu\u00acmmulla, Bandarawela and Haputale Divisional Secretariat Divisions of Badulla District.\n\nPresident Dissanayake also presented a symbolic gift to Army Commander Lieutenant General Nilantha Premaratne in appreciation of the Sri Lanka Army Corps of Engineers\u2019 contribution to the construction of the housing project.\n\nAddressing the gathering, President Dissanayake said the Malayagam community had contributed to building Sri Lanka\u2019s economy for more than 200 years and should be recognised as part of the country.\n\n\u201cThe Malayagam community, who have contributed to building our country\u2019s economy for more than 200 years, are our own people. Where they came from and when they came here are not important. That is history,\u201d he said.\n\nHe noted that despite having lived in Sri Lanka for more than two centuries, many members of the community still lacked ownership of land and their own homes."
