    "md5": "602c23b1c575e902a50e422e34e237a1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1944,
    "chunk_text": "CSE returns to gains as foreign buying supports a volatile session\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange returned to positive territory on Friday, 28 August 2026, with both benchmark indices closing marginally higher following a volatile trading session and a return of foreign buying.\n\nThe All Share Price Index gained 36.26 points, or 0.17%, to close at 21,315.91, while the S&P Sri Lanka 20 Index advanced by 10.53 points, or 0.18%, to end the session at 6,005.34.\n\nThe ASPI opened around the 21,320 level and climbed sharply during early trading before giving up most of its gains as selling pressure emerged towards midday. The index briefly moved close to the 21,300 level before recovering during the afternoon and finishing the session in positive territory.\n\nTotal market turnover reached LKR 2.20 billion, with approximately 66.46 million shares changing hands during the day.\n\nThe Utilities sector dominated market activity, generating approximately LKR 501.90 million in turnover from 13.37 million shares. WindForce accounted for the majority of sector activity, recording approximately LKR 494.85 million in turnover.\n\nCrossing transactions contributed approximately LKR 160.31 million, representing around 7% of total equity turnover. The largest crossing was recorded in Softlogic Capital, where 6.67 million shares changed hands at LKR 11.00, generating approximately LKR 73.34 million. Hatton National Bank and John Keells Holdings also recorded crossings valued at LKR 66.88 million and LKR 20.09 million, respectively.\n\nForeign investor activity provided additional support to the session, with foreign investors turning net buyers and recording a net foreign inflow of LKR 25.99 million.\n\nMarket breadth remained marginally positive, with 108 securities advancing against 102 decliners, resulting in an advance-to-decline ratio of 1.06. This reflected relatively balanced market participation despite gains in both benchmark indices."
