    "chunk_size_bytes": 927,
    "chunk_text": "PM Harini hails Vasudeva Nanayakkara\u2019s contribution to Sri Lanka\u2019s left-wing politics\n\nColombo, Aug. 28 (Daily Mirror) - Prime Minister Harini Amarasuriya has described veteran politician and former Parliamentarian Vasudeva Nanayakkara as an important figure in Sri Lanka\u2019s left-wing political history.\n\nThe Prime Minister made the remarks while attending the launch of a book documenting Nanayakkara\u2019s political life and contribution.\n\nRecalling her time in Parliament alongside Nanayakkara, Amarasuriya said that although they had agreed on certain issues and held differing political views on others, she had always respected his contribution to the country\u2019s left-wing political movement.\n\nShe also recalled engaging in conversations with Nanayakkara about his long political career and experiences.\n\n\u201cFuture generations should know about figures like him who made an impact on Sri Lankan politics,\u201d she said."
