    "chunk_text": "According to the statistics issued by the very NCRS, three-wheelers are not the vehicles\u00a0 involved in the greatest number of road accidents. Motorbikes top the lists of total road accidents as well as\u00a0 fatal accidents for the past several years. This factor has been confirmed by the statistics issued by the NCRS as well as the police.\n\nIn fact,\u00a0 governments in the past considered imposing this age limit ignoring the livelihood of over four million people, as it came without entailing any alternative for\u00a0 people who relied purely on this income.\n\nThe current government seems to have realised this aspect. Deputy Minister Hewage says a vocational training campaign is already been in place, intending to steer young people away from\u00a0 three-wheeler driving and encourage them to pursue skill-based careers. He has stated that once vocational pathways were firmly established, the Government planned to introduce a minimum age requirement of 40 for three-wheeler drivers."
