    "chunk_text": "Namal questions government over delays in Sri Lanka\u2019s Digital ID rollout\n\nColombo, August 29 (Daily Mirror)- Claiming that the deadline for the implementation of Sri Lanka\u2019s Digital ID has now passed, Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) MP Namal Rajapaksa said that the Government must tell the people clearly when the Digital ID actually would be delivered.\n\nThe MP said for nearly two years, the Government has announced successive timelines for the implementation of Sri Lanka\u2019s Digital ID.\n\n\"April 2026 was announced as a target. That deadline has now passed, and we are once again being told that the first Digital ID will be issued by the end of this year.\n\nHow many more deadlines must the people wait through?,\" the asked.\n\nHe said in a post on X that Digital transformation requires more than announcements and that it requires delivery, accountability and timelines that are honoured.\n\n\"The Government must tell the people clearly: When will the Digital ID actually be delivered?, he asked."
