    "md5": "7afb1b867a7f09ae7d677cbc1c8c08ab",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1989,
    "chunk_text": "At least 37 dead and hundreds evacuated after strike on Kyiv weapons depot\n\n(BBC) - Thirty-seven people have died and almost 400 evacuated after a Russian drone strike hit a depot storing weapons for Ukraine's military near a residential area.\n\nPresident Volodymyr Zelensky said the strike caused shells, mines and drones to detonate late on Friday, triggering a blast which damaged nearby properties including a \"care home for elderly people and people with disabilities\".\n\nAn investigation into the \"terrible negligence on the part of those who stored explosive right next to people\" has begun, he said.\n\nFour children are among 42 people injured, according to regional head Tymur Tkachenko, with a rescue operation ongoing at the site in the Bucha district on Saturday.\n\n\"Criminal proceedings have been opened on charges of official negligence,\" Zelensky said.\n\nThe office of Ukraine's prosecutor general earlier said it was reviewing the \"legality of the placement and storage of explosive objects and materials\" near residential buildings in the village of Myla, to the west of the capital Kyiv.\n\nIt said the \"actions of officials who made the relevant decisions\" would also be investigated.\n\nRussia's Ministry of Defence said in a statement that its forces had targeted \"an ammunition depot\" in Myla which stored \"components and launch boosters for FP-1/FP-2 long-range unmanned aerial vehicles\".\n\nMeanwhile, Tkachenko said a 14-year-old was killed in a separate attack in the Boryspil district while Kyiv Mayor Vitaliy Klitschko said a two-year-old had died after a Russian drone crashed in Obolonskyi.\n\nHe added that five people, including an 18-year-old girl, were injured in fresh strikes on the capital on Saturday morning. Five people have been killed across the country over the past day, according to local officials.\n\nZelensky reported further overnight strikes in Odesa, Dnipropetrovsk, Sumy and Zaporizhzhia, as the Ukrainian army said it had shot down 233 Russian drones."
