    "chunk_text": "Dutch health institute issues \u2019red alert\u2019 over Trump-shaped ecstasy pills\n\n(BBC) - A Dutch drug addiction and mental health institute has issued a \"red alert\" to users about potentially lethal ecstasy pills which resemble US President Donald Trump.\n\nThe Utrecht-based Trimbos Institute said several of the pills had been handed in at testing centres in August and were found to contain a \"very high\" amount of the chemical PMMA.\n\n\"Do not use this pill under any circumstance,\" the institute said in its warning, cautioning that the drug could cause \"overheating with potentially fatal consequences\".\n\nIt issued images of the pills, which feature a depiction of Trump's face on one side and the words \"Trump\" and \"NL\" stamped on the other.\n\nPMMA, or para-methoxymethamfetamine, is a substance similar to MDMA \u2013 the active ingredient in ecstasy pills.\n\n\"However, the effect occurs later, and the stimulating effect is often absent,\" the health institute advised. \"This increases the risk of overdose.\"\n\nUsers are being warned they could experience symptoms such as nausea, an increased heart rate and convulsions hours after ingesting the pills.\n\nTrimbos Institute spokesperson Anniek Groothuis told the Associated Press that it had no reported cases of death or serious illness among possible users.\n\nWhile producing, selling and using ecstasy is illegal in the Netherlands, a 2024 Dutch government report said the substance was \"still quite popular as a party drug\".\n\nThe report added that, in 2022, a \"record 550,000 people\" had taken the drug at least once.\n\nThis is not the first time Donald Trump's facial features appear to have been used as inspiration for the shape of ecstasy pills.\n\nIn 2017, German police confiscated about 5,000 carrot-coloured ecstasy tablets in the shape of the US president's head \u2013 which they believed had been promoted on the internet under the slogan \"Trump makes partying great again\"."
