    "chunk_size_bytes": 569,
    "chunk_text": "Fire breaks out at Embilipitiya Paper Mill\n\nColombo, Aug. 30 (Daily Mirror) - A fire broke out this afternoon (30) at a warehouse used to store waste materials within the premises of the Embilipitiya Paper Mill.\n\nThe fire was reported at around 3.20 p.m. and prompted a joint response involving the paper mill\u2019s fire unit, the Sri Lanka Army, Police, Embilipitiya Urban Council and the Sevenagala Sugar Factory fire brigade.\n\nAuthorities worked together to prevent the blaze from spreading to other areas of the facility and eventually brought the fire under control."
  },
  {
