    "md5": "b63e93f66c107a7eb9cc6ad083b7d088",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2000,
    "chunk_text": "INSEE Cement launches Galle training school\n\nDelivers Mason\u2019s Upskilling NVQ Level 3 Programme to advance recognition and opportunities for masons\n\n\u200bINSEE Cement, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading and only fully integrated cement manufacturer, with flagship brands INSEE Sanstha and Mahaweli Marine Plus, opened a dedicated training school at its Galle plant recently, to deliver the Mason\u2019s Upskilling NVQ Level 3 Programme, a pioneering project designed to formally recognise and elevate the skills of the country\u2019s experienced masons.\n\nThe Mason Training School was ceremonially opened by INSEE Cement Chairman Nandana Ekanayake, INSEE Cement CEO Eng. Thusith Gunawarnasuriya and Chamber of Construction Industry of Sri Lanka (CCI) Secretary General and CEO Eng. Col. Nissanka N. Wijeratne, together with the senior members of the INSEE Cement and CCI teams.\n\nThe programme was developed under a memorandum of understanding between INSEE Cement, the CCI and Tertiary and Vocational Education Commission (TVEC).\n\nUnlike the conventional training courses, it adopts the Recognition of Prior Learning methodology, which assesses and validates the practical knowledge the masons have gained over many years, enabling them to obtain a nationally recognised vocational qualification.\n\nThrough the process, 100 selected masons from the Galle and Puttalam region will be awarded the NVQ Level 3 certification as the first phrase of the programme. The facilities within the INSEE Cement Galle plant have been specially prepared to host the training and assessment, ensuring a safe and effective learning environment.\n\nEach partner has a distinct role in delivering the programme. INSEE Cement will identify and select the masons and provide facilities, equipment, safety measures and technical expertise. The CCI is delivering vocational training, managing assessments and coordinating with the TVEC. The TVEC will set the required national standards, supervise training and issue the NVQ Level 3 certificates."
  },
