    "md5": "15f0f988f885fcf2961fe4bdb6ff3385",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1333,
    "chunk_text": "Each partner has a distinct role in delivering the programme. INSEE Cement will identify and select the masons and provide facilities, equipment, safety measures and technical expertise. The CCI is delivering vocational training, managing assessments and coordinating with the TVEC. The TVEC will set the required national standards, supervise training and issue the NVQ Level 3 certificates.\n\nEng. Gunawarnasuriya said, \u201cWe are proud to partner the CCI and TVEC on this important initiative. Sincere thanks to both organisations for their close collaboration in bringing the programme to life. Upskilling and formally recognising the masons who have long been the backbone of the construction industry is something we are deeply proud to support. INSEE Cement looks forward to extending the opportunity to more masons as the programme expands to Puttalam.\u201d\n\nFollowing the successful completion of the Galle phase, the initiative will expand to Puttalam, with the necessary arrangements to be planned over the next two months and the second phase expected to commence thereafter.\n\nExtending the opportunity to the masons in multiple regions, INSEE Cement and its partners aim to uplift the workforce, improve construction practices and contribute to Sri Lanka\u2019s socioeconomic progress through skill development and recognition."
