    "md5": "d24d60e396bdf8735661e5151b5e0d33",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1742,
    "chunk_text": "SLCHBC celebrates 25th anniversary, reaffirms commitment to bilateral trade\n\nThe Executive Committee of the Sri Lanka\u2013China Business Council together with its Past Presidents\n\nThe Sri Lanka\u2013China Business Council (SLCHBC) of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce recently celebrated its 25th anniversary, marking a quarter-century of economic and trade cooperation between Sri Lanka and China.\n\nThe event, themed \u201c25 Years of Unwavering Alliance,\u201d brought together senior government officials, diplomats, past presidents and office-bearers of the Council, and prominent business leaders from both countries, including Krishan Balendra, Chairperson of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of John Keells Holdings PLC, and Wang Gang, Chairman of the Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Sri Lanka and Managing Director of China Harbour Engineering Company.\n\nWasantha Samarasinghe, Minister of Trade, Commerce, Food Security, and Cooperative Development, attended as the Chief Guest. In his address, the Minister hailed the strong economic relations between the two countries.\n\nNoting that China remained Sri Lanka\u2019s largest import partner in 2025, with iron and steel, knitted fabrics and vehicles among the top imports, while Sri Lankan exports to China included apparel, tea, activated carbon, vegetable fibre, coconut husk chips, etc. He also encouraged strengthened partnerships to continue enhancing trade between the two countries, and reaffirmed the Government\u2019s commitment to a stable, transparent and investor-friendly business environment.\n\nSunil Handunnetti, Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development and Chathuranga Abeysinghe, Deputy Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development, also attended the event."
