    "md5": "c37e3a1834a021e1c0eab1612321021c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1752,
    "chunk_text": "Regional leaders pledge to step up sustainable finance at UN SDG Investment Forum\n\nAs part of Forward Faster Now | APAC 2026, the UN Global Compact Network Sri Lanka convened the SDG Investment Forum, a high-level Technical Deep Dive and Leadership Roundtable dedicated to advancing sustainable and transition finance across Asia-Pacific emerging markets.\n\nDelivered in collaboration with the United Nations Environment Programme Finance Initiative (UNEP FI), the Principles for Responsible Investment (PRI) and the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI), the Forum brought together senior leaders from the financial sector, institutional investors, impact investors, corporates, development finance institutions, regulators,sustainability practitioners and development partners to explore how finance can accelerate progress towards the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\n\nThe SDG Investment Forum was supported by Principal Corporate Partners Sampath Bank, Hatton National Bank (HNB) and Hayleys PLC, alongside Supporting Corporate Partners Amana Bank and Dialog Axiata PLC, demonstrating strong private sector leadership and commitment to advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s sustainable finance agenda.\n\nThe invitation-only forum explored one of the defining questions facing the region today: Can emerging markets better position themselves and bridge the intermediation gap to attract the capital needed to accelerate sustainable development and deliver on the SDGs?\n\nThe Forum highlighted that achieving the SDGs requires more than ambition\u2014it demands stronger collaboration between capital providers and businesses, alongside credible transition strategies, transparent governance and investable pipelines capable of unlocking private finance at scale."
