    "language": "en",
    "md5": "eae93b9345af668898ee7e2ba256680f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1550,
    "chunk_text": "The Forum highlighted that achieving the SDGs requires more than ambition\u2014it demands stronger collaboration between capital providers and businesses, alongside credible transition strategies, transparent governance and investable pipelines capable of unlocking private finance at scale.\n\nDiscussions also emphasized the importance of regional cooperation, blended finance, and strengthening investor confidence to mobilize greater levels of sustainable investment into emerging markets.\n\nKeynote addresses from Nathan Fabian, Chief Sustainable Systems Officer at PRI, and Nirnita Talukdar, Asia Pacific Lead at UNEP FI, provided valuable insights into how investors assess transition opportunities and how financial institutions are embedding sustainability into investment and financing decisions. The speakers explored the importance of transparency, robust disclosure, fiduciary responsibility, and innovative financing mechanisms in scaling capital towards climate-resilient and inclusive economies.\n\nThe programme then transitioned into a series of four technical deep dives, deliberately sequenced to build on one another rather than stand alone. Rebecca Kwee, Associate Director at LeapFrog Investments, opened with a case study on how impact-oriented capital is deployed across emerging Asia and what portfolio companies and local partners must demonstrate to attract it. Yixi (Wilson) Wei, Investment Manager Assistant and Chief Analyst of ESG at E Fund Management, followed with an additional case study from the investor\u2019s perspective."
  },
  {
