    "md5": "0a30a83266a0885d1f4ad33c150c5b7e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1517,
    "chunk_text": "Throughout the discussions, participants explored several priority themes shaping the future of sustainable finance, including transition finance instruments, blended finance, sustainable disclosure frameworks, internal carbon pricing and strategies for communicating sustainability in an evolving global investment landscape. These conversations reinforced that mobilizing capital at the scale required will depend on stronger partnerships between investors, businesses, policymakers, and development institutions.\n\nThe SDG Investment Forum forms part of Forward Faster Now | APAC 2026, hosted by the UN Global Compact Network Sri Lanka in partnership with the UN Global Compact Asia & Oceania Regional Team and Country Networks across the region. Together, these platforms reaffirm the UN Global Compact\u2019s commitment to equipping businesses with the knowledge, partnerships, and practical solutions needed to accelerate progress towards the SDGs.\n\nBy convening leaders from across the investment ecosystem, the SDG Investment Forum demonstrated that sustainable finance is not only essential to addressing today\u2019s environmental and social challenges, but also a strategic driver of long-term resilience, competitiveness and inclusive economic growth. Through continued collaboration under the one-year Sustainable Finance Implementation Workplan, the partnerships established through the Forum will help accelerate the flow of capital needed to deliver a more sustainable and prosperous future for Asia-Pacific."
  },
