    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "21dc51f22c92bae1333923549cf1607a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1737,
    "chunk_text": "Building on experience and lessons learnt over the last cycles of cohorts and entrepreneurship support provision, EthicalX aims to provide the new cohort with a holistic package of support building on needs identified by entrepreneurs and stakeholders. This includes financial support for selected ventures, with support for lifestyle-focused entrepreneurs provided in partnership with c.fuge.\n\n\u201cEthicalX builds long-term relationships with entrepreneurs and helps to create the conditions they need to develop and grow their ideas,\u201d he added.\n\nSharing her experience as an EthicalX cohort member, Nimasha Perera, Co-founder of Star Mushrooms, said: \u201cThrough EthicalX, we have built valuable connections with entrepreneurs and others working on sustainable solutions. The mentorship and guidance we received have supported our business journey and created opportunities to learn from others facing similar challenges.\u201d\n\nFor Nilushi Thenuwara of Eastern Soy Products, another EthicalX cohort member, those connections have also led to new collaborations. \u201cAs a family business, opportunities to connect and collaborate through EthicalX have been really valuable. One of these connections has been with a chef and we are now working together to develop recipes as we prepare to expand our range of soy-based products.\u201d\n\nThe launch event brought together entrepreneurs, mentors, representatives from the public sector, the private sector, and other ecosystem actors to exchange experiences, discuss common challenges, and explore opportunities for collaboration and future partnerships.\n\nThe 2026 cohort will focus and support entrepreneurs working in sustainable food systems, fashion and lifestyle, and creative communication."
  },
