    "md5": "2dc9a6d664bc4ff7703f23e403fa3285",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1792,
    "chunk_text": "Digital Summit Asia to position Sri Lanka as Regional Digital Hub\n\nThe Digital Marketing Association of Sri Lanka (DMASL) has officially announced the return of Digital Summit Asia \u2013 Sri Lanka 2026, taking place from 1\u20132 October at Water\u2019s Edge, Colombo, with an exclusive C-Suite Event on 30 September.\n\nReturning with a renewed regional identity and expanded international vision, the summit will bring together Asia\u2019s leading marketers, creators, innovators, entrepreneurs, technology leaders, policymakers, and digital professionals to exchange ideas, build partnerships, and shape the future of the digital economy.\n\nBuilding on the success of previous editions, Digital Summit Asia \u2013 Sri Lanka 2026 strengthens Sri Lanka\u2019s position as a regional destination for digital innovation, collaboration, and thought leadership.\n\nThis year\u2019s summit will be held under the theme \u201cThe Epicentre. A Mind That Forms.\u201d\u00a0 Reflecting the belief that transformative ideas are born when diverse minds, industries, and cultures come together to challenge convention, exchange perspectives, and inspire progress.\n\nDigital Summit Asia aims to become that epicentre, where conversations spark collaboration, ideas evolve into action, and innovation drives the future of Asia\u2019s digital economy.\n\nAs Asia continues to lead global advancements in technology, creativity, and digital transformation, Digital Summit Asia \u2013 Sri Lanka 2026 seeks to strengthen cross-border collaboration while positioning Sri Lanka as a strategic meeting point for the region\u2019s digital ecosystem.\n\nThe summit will feature an exciting lineup of regional and international speakers alongside Sri Lanka\u2019s leading industry experts, creating opportunities for learning, networking, and long-term collaboration."
  },
