    "md5": "60d20a8604017f8be5d9d3c3a87474f0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1484,
    "chunk_text": "Melbourne-Colombo flights already running near-full, beating expectations: Jetstar\u2019s Zeglin\n\nMelbourne-Colombo flights already over 90% full each way, even outside peak season: Zeglin\n\nJetstar taps Intrepid Travel tie-up to unlock Australia\u2019s leisure potential beyond its VFR-heavy visitor base\n\nJetstar Airways\u2019 inaugural Melbourne\u2013Colombo flight touched down at Bandaranaike International Airport last week to a ceremony marking the airline\u2019s entry into the Sri Lankan market.\n\nSpeaking to Daily Mirror Business on the sidelines of the event, Jetstar Airways Executive Manager Commercial Scott Zeglin said demand on the new route has already outpaced the airline\u2019s own forecasts, even outside peak season.\n\n\u201cWe were 92 percent full coming in, and 91 percent on the way out today. What we have noticed is that the flights have a good baseline load, but then they book really late too. With this inaugural flight, we were surprised how full it got, we weren\u2019t expecting it to be this full, but it has been very, very strong,\u201d Zeglin said.\n\nThe service, operated with a reconfigured widebody Boeing 787-8 Dreamliner, runs three times weekly year-round and introduces more than 100,000 low-fare seats annually on the corridor, establishing Sri Lanka\u2019s first low-cost direct link to Australia, though SriLankan Airlines already operates the route on a full-service basis. Jetstar\u2019s pitch is squarely on price, with promotional launch fares starting from Rs. 67,770."
  },
