    "chunk_text": "The push aligns with World Bank\u2019s wider engagement in the two provinces, including its REVIVE programme covering Jaffna, Pasikuda, Trincomalee and Arugam Bay under the government\u2019s Tourism Strategic Plan 2026-2030, and a separate US$ 100 million loan facility the Cabinet approved in August for broader regional development.\n\nWevita\u2019s comments mark one of his first major public remarks on arrivals since assuming the SLTDA chairmanship on August 18, succeeding Buddhika Hewawasam, who continues to lead the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau (SLTPB) under a restructured leadership arrangement announced by the Tourism Ministry. Sri Lanka recorded a record 2,362,521 tourist arrivals in 2025, generating around US$ 3.2 billion in revenue; the full-year revenue target for 2026 has since been revised to approximately US$ 4.2 billion."
