    "md5": "4ee536af400cd911907e70b89fc48cf1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1111,
    "chunk_text": "Three-Wheeler Fares in  Nuwara Eliya\n\nThree-wheeler drivers in Nuwara Eliya appear to be having a field day, with minimum fares reportedly around Rs. 400. Foreign tourists may be charged even more.\n\nIt is not unusual to see tourists bargaining with drivers and, at times, arguments taking place over fares. This can create a very negative impression of Sri Lanka at a time when tourism income is important to our economy and the country is making every effort to attract more visitors.\n\nOne of the main issues is the absence of metered three-wheelers in Nuwara Eliya. Passengers are therefore left to negotiate the fare before every journey.\n\nThe relevant authorities should intervene without delay and regulate the industry by making fare meters compulsory and ensuring that reasonable charges are displayed and enforced.\n\nNuwara Eliya is one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading tourist destinations. We should not allow unreasonable transport fares and unpleasant arguments to damage the image of our country.\n\nThe time has come for the authorities to act before serious damage is done to Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism industry."
  },
