    "chunk_size_bytes": 1879,
    "chunk_text": "Reflections on Dr. Dayan Jayatilleka\u2019s \u201cFake left matrix: Five false doctrines misleading Sri Lanka\u201d\n\nIt is with much despair that I opt to express my opinion regarding an article that was published in the Daily FT on 6 August 2026, which was boldly titled as mentioned above.\n\nBefore proceeding further, I must acknowledge that I am an ordinary octogenarian whose contemporaries have mostly departed from this world, and whose personal details would not interest anyone.\n\nPrior to expanding on the \u201c\ufb01ve false doctrines misleading Sri Lanka\u201d, the writer makes the authoritative assertion that \u201cSri Lanka is headed for another calamitous cycle towards the end of this decade because of the simple failure, unwillingness or inability of our society \u2013 especially its intelligentsia \u2013 to think through these currently dominant false doctrines.\u201d\n\nI pity the intelligentsia, let alone the gullible ordinary citizens like you and me, for their mediocre abilities. Is it fair to demean the abilities of the responsible citizens of this country in this manner? There are and have been exceptionally brilliant and resourceful intellectuals who serve the country and its children, as opposed to endorsing the political elite who are amusingly said to be blessed with economic prowess due to their assembly line of a bloodline. We cannot broadly judge the ability, credibility, and sincerity of our intelligentsia in this belligerent manner.\n\nOut of the \u2018\ufb01ve false doctrines\u2019 currently misleading Sri Lanka, as professed by the writer, at the moment the \ufb01rst one is as follows: \u201cCorruption is the main problem and root cause of the economic crisis. Combating corruption is and should be the main priority.\u201d The writer disagrees and declares \u201cCorruption and its elimination have never been the top priority in the history of political or economic thought.\u201d"
