    "chunk_text": "Out of the \u2018\ufb01ve false doctrines\u2019 currently misleading Sri Lanka, as professed by the writer, at the moment the \ufb01rst one is as follows: \u201cCorruption is the main problem and root cause of the economic crisis. Combating corruption is and should be the main priority.\u201d The writer disagrees and declares \u201cCorruption and its elimination have never been the top priority in the history of political or economic thought.\u201d\n\nI further wonder whether loan-granting international institutions would ever endorse corruption and misuse of their funds. As far as I understand, institutions such as IMF, ADB, UNESCO, UNFAO would expect clean hands of the receiver of those funds because such aid is meant to relieve the sweat and sacrifices of citizens as opposed to lining the coffers of the political elite. Such foreign aid constitutes the money of foreign taxpayers and must be untouched by the taint of domestic corruption, speaking from a purely ethical standpoint. Therefore, transparency and accountability of the handling of such funds received as loans or aid is mandatory for building public trust in the Government of Sri Lanka, both domestically and internationally. The rulers are temporary workers for the State and not owners of the country. The State is permanent and the Government is temporary, whether it\u2019s JVP/NPP or any other. They must fulfil promises, failing which they must loosen the reins and retreat with dignity."
