    "chunk_text": "Prime Minister departs for Bhutan\n\nColombo, Aug. 31 (Daily Mirror) - Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya departed Sri Lanka today for an official visit to Bhutan, where she is scheduled to participate in the Global Conscious Food Systems Summit.\n\nThe summit is scheduled to take place in Bhutan, with Prime Minister Amarasuriya set to participate in the opening plenary tomorrow, September 1.\n\nAccording to the Prime Minister\u2019s Office, she will deliver a keynote address under the theme \u201cRising to the Moment: Igniting Consciousness to Address the Polycrisis.\u201d\n\nDuring her visit, the Prime Minister is also expected to hold discussions with international leaders and representatives on strengthening cooperation in sustainable food systems, food security and the development of resilient communities."
