    "chunk_size_bytes": 1660,
    "chunk_text": "Former Minister Ravi Karunanayake released on bail\n\nColombo, Aug. 31 (Daily Mirror) - Former Finance Minister Ravi Karunanayake, who was arrested by the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption over allegations that three employees recruited for a special project of the National Lotteries Board were deployed for his political activities, causing a loss to the Government, was today ordered to be released on bail by Colombo Additional Magistrate Liyan Warushavithana.\n\nThe Magistrate ordered the suspect to be released on two surties of Rs. 1 million each and also imposed a travel ban on him.\n\nThe order was made after CIABOC officials made submissions when the case relating to the incident was taken up before court.\n\nSuspect, a sitting Member of Parliament, was arrested by CIABOC today when he appeared before the Commission to provide a statement in connection with the investigation.\n\nCIABOC informed court that suspect had been directed on four occasions to appear before the Commission in connection with the investigation, but had failed to do so. As a result, a team of CIABOC officers had visited his residence on August 29 and conducted an inquiry.\n\nThe Commission further informed court that although the suspect had repeatedly requested lengthy postponements despite being directed to appear before the Commission, when CIABOC officers visited his residence, they were informed that he had travelled to the Nuwara Eliya area for his daughter's wedding.\n\nHowever, CIABOC informed court that subsequent investigations had revealed information indicating that the suspect was in the Hambantota area rather than Nuwara Eliya."
