    "chunk_size_bytes": 1928,
    "chunk_text": "The Commission further informed court that although the suspect had repeatedly requested lengthy postponements despite being directed to appear before the Commission, when CIABOC officers visited his residence, they were informed that he had travelled to the Nuwara Eliya area for his daughter's wedding.\n\nHowever, CIABOC informed court that subsequent investigations had revealed information indicating that the suspect was in the Hambantota area rather than Nuwara Eliya.\n\nThe officers alleged that the three individuals had been recruited under the pretext of being attached to a special project of the Ministry of Finance, while they had allegedly performed no services for the National Lotteries Board.\n\nNevertheless, the NLB had allegedly paid their salaries and allowances, resulting in a financial loss to the institution.\n\nCIABOC further informed court that the suspect had acted together with the first suspect to influence witnesses and requested that he be remanded in custody.\n\nCharges had been filed against the former Finance Minister for allegedly committing the offence of corruption under Section 70 of the Bribery Act, as amended by Act No. 20 of 1994.\n\nAppearing for the suspect, Senior Counsel Asoka Weerasooriya requested that his client be granted bail, submitting that suspect was suffering from several medical conditions.\n\n\"Your Honour, my client currently has five stents. The medical reports relating to an examination conducted at a hospital in Singapore on August 26, 2026, state that there is a possibility of placing three more stents in the future. My client also suffers from sleep apnoea. He has also been infected with cellulitis, a serious bacterial infection, and therefore cannot stay in unhygienic environments.\u201d\n\nHe further submitted that Dr. Gotabhaya Ranasinghe had prescribed medication that his client was required to take daily and that he was also receiving insulin for diabetes."
