    "chunk_text": "Tourism and worker remittances are enormously important. But a modern economy cannot depend indefinitely on tourism, remittances and external borrowing to finance its ambitions.\n\nThe country must aggressively expand higher-value export oriented manufacturing. And economic diplomacy must become part of that national export strategy.\n\nThere is another lesson from 2022 that Sri Lanka must never forget.\n\nGovernments make major decisions based on the information and advice placed before them.\n\nTherefore, economists, officials, advisers and institutions occupying influential positions carry enormous responsibility.\n\nSri Lanka cannot afford advisers who tell political leaders what they want to hear merely to preserve their positions, influence or relevance.\n\nEconomic advice must serve the country\u2014not the careers of those giving it.\n\nThe most valuable adviser is sometimes the person prepared to walk into the room and say. \u201cNo. This will not work.\u201d\n\nSri Lanka paid an enormous economic and social price when warning signs were ignored, uncomfortable realities were postponed and difficult decisions were avoided.\n\nThis Government must insist on evidence, accountability and intellectual honesty from those advising it.\n\nThe objective cannot be to recreate Sri Lanka 2019 or Sri Lanka 2021. The objective must be to create a fundamentally more competitive Sri Lanka for 2030 and beyond.\n\nRecovery is not simply when reserves rise. It is when exports and productive industries continuously generate foreign exchange. Recovery is not simply when government revenue rises. It is when businesses grow, wages rise and prosperity naturally expands the tax base. Recovery is not simply when credit ratings improve. It is when global investors trust Sri Lanka enough to commit billions in long-term capital. Recovery is not simply when GDP returns to its pre-crisis size. It is when families regain purchasing power and businesses regain the confidence to invest, hire and expand."
