    "language": "en",
    "md5": "572f93b0584d5815e2679ef8fc2f44d1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 986,
    "chunk_text": "CSE snaps three-month losing streak in August, down 5.7% YTD\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) returned to positive territory in August, with both benchmark indices posting their first monthly gains since April, snapping three consecutive months of declines.\n\nYear-to-date, the ASPI had declined 5.68% and the active S&P SL20 was down 2.4%.\n\nThe ASPI gained 0.99% during August, while the S&P SL20 rose 1.17%, reversing part of July\u2019s 5.09% and 4.27% losses, respectively.\n\nThe rebound follows a weak three-month stretch from May through July for the ASPI, while the S&P SL20 declined in May and July with only a marginal 0.75% gain in June.\n\nThe August gains nevertheless remain modest compared with the swings seen earlier in the year, when both indices rose strongly in January and April but suffered their steepest monthly declines in March.\n\nThe trend marks a contrast with the second half of 2025, when the ASPI recorded six consecutive monthly gains from July through December."
  },
