    "chunk_text": "Ravi Karunanayake released on bail in NLB corruption case\n\nFormer Finance Minister and New Democratic Front (NDF) MP Ravi Karunanayake, who was arrested by the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC) over allegations that three employees recruited for a special project of the National Lotteries Board (NLB) were deployed for his political activities, causing a loss to the Government, was yesterday ordered to be released on bail by Colombo Additional Magistrate Liyan Warushavithana.\n\nThe Magistrate ordered the suspect to be released on two sureties of Rs. 1 million each and also imposed a travel ban on him.\n\nKarunanayake was arrested when he appeared before CIABOC to provide a statement in connection with the investigation.\n\nCIABOC told court that the case concerned three employees recruited on contract during Karunanayake\u2019s tenure as Finance Minister from 12 January 2015 to 22 May 2017.\n\nInvestigators alleged that Karunanayake, together with then NLB Chairman Shyamala Perera, recruited two Coordinating Officers and a Management Assistant using NLB funds, purportedly for a special project of the Finance Ministry.\n\nCIABOC alleged that the three employees performed no services for the NLB but were paid salaries and allowances by the institution, resulting in a financial loss. It alleged that they had instead been deployed for Karunanayake\u2019s political activities.\n\nThe Commission sought his remand, alleging that he had acted together with the first suspect to influence witnesses.\n\nCIABOC also told court that Karunanayake had been directed on four occasions to appear before the Commission but had failed to do so. Officers subsequently visited his residence on 29 August to conduct an inquiry.\n\nAccording to CIABOC, officers were informed that Karunanayake had travelled to Nuwara Eliya for his daughter\u2019s wedding, but subsequent investigations indicated that he was in Hambantota."
