    "chunk_text": "CIABOC also told court that Karunanayake had been directed on four occasions to appear before the Commission but had failed to do so. Officers subsequently visited his residence on 29 August to conduct an inquiry.\n\nAccording to CIABOC, officers were informed that Karunanayake had travelled to Nuwara Eliya for his daughter\u2019s wedding, but subsequent investigations indicated that he was in Hambantota.\n\nAppearing for Karunanayake, Senior Counsel Asoka Weerasooriya sought bail on medical grounds and told court that his client had five stents and could require three more, citing medical reports from an examination in Singapore on 26 August. He also cited sleep apnoea, cellulitis and diabetes.\n\nCounsel also submitted that the first suspect had already been granted bail and that there was no reason for Karunanayake to evade court proceedings.\n\nAfter considering the submissions, the Additional Magistrate ordered Karunanayake\u2019s release on bail."
