    "md5": "d2bd3e337ae95a3ef108f2462a59fd86",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1432,
    "chunk_text": "It also alleges that Justice Yasantha Kodagoda, who had been the senior-most judge of the previous bench and was involved in preparing the judgement, was removed from the case without a valid legal reason.\n\nThe complaint alleges that the same bench ordered the termination of proceedings on that day, contrary to established judicial practice.\n\nDr Sanjeewa claims that the order prevented the recovery of approximately US$999 million that could have been obtained from the company and its representatives and also affected the work of the Compensation Management Commission appointed by the court.\n\nA letter dated March 6, 2026, had reportedly informed the petitioners that the commission could no longer continue its work as a result of the court order, the complaint states.\n\nDr Sanjeewa has requested CIABOC to investigate the allegations under the Anti-Corruption Act No. 9 of 2023.\n\nHe has alleged that the conduct attributed to the three judges could amount to an act of corruption involving the misuse of public office under Section 111 of the Act.\n\nThe complaint calls for an independent and credible investigation, appropriate legal action if wrongdoing is established, and notification of the progress of the investigation in accordance with Section 44 of the Act.\n\nThe allegations contained in the complaint have not been independently established, and the judges named in it have not been found guilty of any wrongdoing."
