    "chunk_text": "National Youth Innovation Challenge launched to mark World Food Day\n\nFrom left: Dihan Hettige - Assistant FAO Representative (Administration), Vimlendra Sharan -\u00a0 FAO Representative for Sri Lanka and the Maldives, Damith Pallewatte - Managing Director of Hatton National Bank PLC, Priyanka Wijayaratne - Senior Vice President / Chief Sustainability Officer HNB, Deepal Udukumbura - Vice President of Agribusiness HNB and Shanel Perera - Assistant Manager, Sustainable Business after the signing ceremony\n\nThe Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO), in partnership with the Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education and Hatton National Bank (HNB), launched the World Food Day 2026 Youth Innovation Challenge, a nationwide competition that invites university students to develop innovative solutions to address some of Sri Lanka\u2019s most pressing agrifood systems challenges.\n\nWorld Food Day is observed annually on 16 October to commemorate the founding of FAO in 1945. Celebrated in more than 150 countries, it raises awareness of the importance of food security, nutrition and sustainable agrifood systems while promoting collective action to ensure healthy diets for all.\n\nHeld under the World Food Day 2026 theme, \u201cInnovate Today \u2013 Nourish Tomorrow,\u201d the initiative seeks to harness the creativity, knowledge and entrepreneurial spirit of young people to generate practical, scalable solutions that contribute to more efficient, resilient and sustainable agrifood systems."
  },
  {
