    "md5": "eee1e8b47ec21755b134878bdee5a9f1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1714,
    "chunk_text": "Lanka Hospitals secures top honours at GlobalHealth Sri Lanka Awards 2026\n\nAt the GlobalHealth Sri Lanka Awards 2026, Lanka Hospitals was named Bariatric Service Provider of the Year in Sri Lanka, Sustainability and CSR Excellence Service Provider of the Year in Sri Lanka, and Medical Tourism Hospital of the Year in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe Bariatric Service Provider of the Year in Sri Lanka award recognises Lanka Hospitals\u2019 position as the country\u2019s leading private hospital for bariatric surgery. Its team has performed the highest number of bariatric surgeries among private hospitals in Sri Lanka, while Lanka Hospitals remains the only centre in the country to have completed 450 successful weight loss procedures. The recognition reflects the expertise of its multidisciplinary medical teams, consistent patient safety standards and continued focus on achieving positive, sustainable outcomes.\n\nRecognition for Sustainability and CSR Excellence is grounded in programmes that extend the hospital\u2019s clinical capabilities to communities. Through Lanka Hospitals Suwa Sathkara, the hospital has responded to public health needs with timely medical interventions. In partnership with the Rotary Clubs of Colombo Metropolitan and Colombo West, Lanka Hospitals facilitated 100 urgent heart surgeries for children, helping them receive essential cardiothoracic care without prolonged delays.\n\nFollowing Cyclone Ditwah, the hospital also established medical clinics and treatment centres in affected areas, providing treatment and relief to communities whose access to healthcare had been disrupted. These initiatives demonstrate how Lanka Hospitals translates social responsibility into meaningful clinical action."
  },
