    "chunk_size_bytes": 1296,
    "chunk_text": "Following Cyclone Ditwah, the hospital also established medical clinics and treatment centres in affected areas, providing treatment and relief to communities whose access to healthcare had been disrupted. These initiatives demonstrate how Lanka Hospitals translates social responsibility into meaningful clinical action.\n\nFollowing this recognition, at the National Business Excellence Awards 2026, Lanka Hospitals was recognised as Joint Winner in the Healthcare, Hospital Sector, and Joint 2nd Runner Up in the Overall Large Category. These two honours place its healthcare performance within the discipline of organisational leadership, governance, operational effectiveness, and sustainable business management.\n\nDr. R. P. Sanjaya Ratnayake, Group Chief Executive Officer of Lanka Hospitals said, \u201cWe are proud of this momentum, but our priority remains unchanged: to provide safe, high quality and patient centred care, while continuing to strengthen the expertise, technology and systems that make better outcomes possible.\u201d\n\nThese five honours provide a strong foundation for the next phase of Lanka Hospitals\u2019 growth. The hospital will carry this momentum forward by setting higher organisational benchmarks and remaining responsive to the evolving expectations of those it serves."
