    "chunk_text": "On a year-on-year basis, however, the non-food items remained the dominant source of inflation, contributing 5.20 percentage points to the overall rate. Transport alone contributed 2.45 percentage points, mainly reflecting the higher fuel prices compared with August 2025.\n\nHousing, water, electricity, gas and other fuels contributed another 1.14 percentage points, while restaurants and hotels added 0.72 percentage points.\n\nSeveral essential food items recorded steep annual increases. The green chillies averaged Rs.1,414.12 a kilogramme, up 178 percent from a year earlier, while the big onion prices rose 67 percent and dried chillies increased 60 percent. The egg prices climbed 35 percent to an average Rs.44.71 each.\n\nThe CCPI rose to 208.8 index points in August, from 208.2 in July and 193.3 a year earlier. The 12-month moving average inflation increased to 3.9 percent, from 3.3 percent, signalling a continued build-up in broader price pressures."
