    "md5": "1570de74384f65ab38c41376940e6dc3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1854,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2013Hong Kong trade and investment opportunities strengthened through strategic collaboration\n\nA major step towards strengthening trade, investment and business linkages between Sri Lanka and Hong Kong was taken with the successful hosting of the \u201cBridging Markets: Unlocking Hong Kong\u2013Sri Lanka Trade and Investment Opportunities\u201d seminar and business networking dinner on 19 August 2026 at the Celestine Ballroom, Cinnamon Life, Colombo.\n\nThe program was organised by the Hong Kong Economic and Trade Office (HKETO) in Jakarta, Invest Hong Kong (InvestHK) and the Hong Kong Trade Development Council (HKTDC), in association with the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) and the National Chamber of Commerce of Sri Lanka (NCCSL). The event brought together over 100 Sri Lankan exporters and business representatives, creating a valuable platform for direct engagement, networking and exploration of new commercial opportunities.\n\nThe participation represented a diverse cross-section of Sri Lanka\u2019s export economy, including companies from the Apparel, Handicrafts, ICT and Software, Boat Building, Gems, Food and Tea sectors. This broad representation demonstrated the depth and diversity of Sri Lanka\u2019s export capabilities and the potential to further expand Sri Lankan products and services into Hong Kong, Mainland China and wider international markets.\n\nThe event provided Sri Lankan businesses with an opportunity to gain first-hand insights into Hong Kong\u2019s role as an international business and investment hub, as well as its connectivity with the Chinese Mainland and global markets. Discussions also focused on investment facilitation, international market expansion, trade fairs, business summits and opportunities for Sri Lankan companies to establish stronger commercial links with Hong Kong and Chinese enterprises."
  },
