    "chunk_size_bytes": 1775,
    "chunk_text": "The event provided Sri Lankan businesses with an opportunity to gain first-hand insights into Hong Kong\u2019s role as an international business and investment hub, as well as its connectivity with the Chinese Mainland and global markets. Discussions also focused on investment facilitation, international market expansion, trade fairs, business summits and opportunities for Sri Lankan companies to establish stronger commercial links with Hong Kong and Chinese enterprises.\n\nThe Chairman emphasised the need to position Sri Lanka as a competitive and reliable trading and investment destination, while leveraging the country\u2019s diverse export capabilities, skilled workforce and strategic location. He also underscored the importance of moving beyond traditional markets and developing stronger connections with dynamic business centers such as Hong Kong, which can serve as an important gateway to Mainland China and the broader Asian region.\n\nThe program also featured presentations by senior representatives of the Hong Kong business and trade promotion ecosystem. Invest Hong Kong, Jakarta Office Head of Business and Talent Attraction/Investment Promotion Hillwan Brahmanda, outlined opportunities for investment facilitation into Hong Kong and the GoGlobal initiative, including the role of Hong Kong in connecting Chinese Mainland enterprises with international markets.\n\nHKTDC Director \u2013 South Asia and Thailand Vian Cheung highlighted how Sri Lankan companies can utilise HKTDC\u2019s extensive network of international trade fairs and business summits to expand their presence in overseas markets. The presentations provided practical insights into potential avenues for Sri Lankan enterprises seeking to internationalise their businesses and build new partnerships."
