    "chunk_text": "HKTDC Director \u2013 South Asia and Thailand Vian Cheung highlighted how Sri Lankan companies can utilise HKTDC\u2019s extensive network of international trade fairs and business summits to expand their presence in overseas markets. The presentations provided practical insights into potential avenues for Sri Lankan enterprises seeking to internationalise their businesses and build new partnerships.\n\nThe networking session that followed enabled Sri Lankan exporters and representatives of the Hong Kong business community to establish new contacts, exchange information and explore potential business partnerships. The strong participation from diverse export sectors demonstrated considerable interest among Sri Lankan businesses in expanding their international footprint.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Export Development Board, through its collaboration with HKETO, InvestHK, HKTDC and other strategic partners, will continue to facilitate opportunities that connect Sri Lankan exporters with international buyers, investors and business networks. Such partnerships are expected to create further opportunities for Sri Lankan enterprises to participate in international trade fairs, business missions, investment programs and targeted business-to-business engagements.\n\nThe successful seminar marked an important platform for deepening Sri Lanka\u2013Hong Kong economic and commercial relations and reaffirmed the commitment of both sides to explore new avenues for trade, investment and business cooperation. With Sri Lanka\u2019s growing export ambitions and Hong Kong\u2019s strategic position as a gateway to Mainland China and international markets, the collaboration presents significant opportunities for Sri Lankan exporters to diversify markets, build international partnerships and expand their global presence."
