    "md5": "b8af953da1fcc6ffe919d80eb7a25377",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1769,
    "chunk_text": "Arctek Innovations achieves International Standards Certification, strengthening commitment to quality and food safety\n\nArctek Innovations has achieved a significant milestone with the successful implementation of internationally recognised management systems covering quality, food safety, good manufacturing practices, and hazard control\n\nArctek Innovations Ltd., a Sri Lankan manufacturer of food-grade adhesive solutions, has achieved compliance with several internationally recognised standards, including ISO 9001:2015 for Quality Management Systems, ISO 22000:2018 for Food Safety Management Systems, Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP), and Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Point (HACCP).\n\nThe certifications cover the company\u2019s operations relating to the manufacturing, packaging, storage, and dispatch of food-grade polymer-based (PVA) and starch-based adhesives for commercial applications. The achievement represents an important step in Arctek Innovations\u2019 ongoing efforts to strengthen its manufacturing capabilities and provide customers with products that consistently meet stringent quality and food safety requirements.\n\nThe achievement reflects the strategic vision and leadership of Sumedha Abeyrathna, Nayomi Rathnayaka, Sanjaya Seneratne, Charitha Perera, whose collective commitment has driven the organisation\u2019s transformation towards greater operational excellence and continual improvement.\n\nThe certification process involved a comprehensive review and strengthening of the company\u2019s operational systems. Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) were established and enhanced, Good Manufacturing Practices were strengthened, HACCP principles were incorporated, and a risk-based approach was introduced across key operational processes."
  },
  {
